{"slug": 'solar-generator-with-panels-included',
 "question": 'G02',
 "method": 'ab-2026-11', "all_links": True, "buy_compare": True,
 "angle": 'E',
 "searched_as": ['best solar generator kits panels included 2026 EcoFlow Jackery Bluetti Anker specifications', 'best solar generator kits panels included EcoFlow Delta 2 Jackery 1000 v2 Bluetti AC180 Anker C1000 specifications 2026', 'best solar generator kits with solar panels included 2026 reviews EcoFlow Jackery Bluetti Anker', 'best solar generator bundles with solar panels included 2026 EcoFlow Jackery Anker Bluetti prices', 'best solar generator kits with solar panels included 2026 EcoFlow Jackery Bluetti Anker comparison', 'best solar generator kits with panels included 2026 EcoFlow Jackery Bluetti Anker specifications comparison'],
 "title": 'Best solar generator with panels included (2026): 15 kits compared on battery, inverter, solar input and price',
 "h1": 'Best solar generator with panels included (2026): 15 kits compared',
 "desc": 'We compared solar generator kits with panels included from BLUETTI, Jackery, EcoFlow and Anker. The comparison covers lab-measured usable energy, measured panel output, AC output, solar input and maker-store prices checked on 2026-11-13.',
 "answer": '<p class="lead"><strong>Short answer.</strong> The best solar generator with panels included is the BLUETTI Elite 200 V2 kit with two 200 W solar panels: StorageReview measured 1,910 Wh delivered from its 2,073.6 Wh battery, the most usable energy of the solar generator kits compared here.</p>',
 "columns": [('usable', 'Measured usable energy'), ('battery', 'Rated battery'), ('panels', 'Panels in the box'), ('per_wh', 'Price per usable Wh'), ('ac', 'AC continuous')],
 "rows": [{'slug': 'bluetti-elite-200-v2-2x200w-solar-kit', 'model': 'BLUETTI Elite 200 V2 + 2 × 200 W', 'cells': {'usable': '1,910 Wh (StorageReview)', 'battery': '2,073.6 Wh', 'panels': '2 × 200 W (SP200L)', 'per_wh': '$0.78', 'ac': '2,600 W'}}, {'brand': 'Jackery', 'model': 'Solar Generator 2000 v2 (Explorer 2000 v2 + 2 × SolarSaga 200 W)', 'url': 'https://www.jackery.com/products/jackery-solar-generator-2000-v2', 'cells': {'usable': '1,710 Wh (OutdoorGearLab)', 'battery': '2,042 Wh', 'panels': '2 × SolarSaga 200 W', 'per_wh': '$0.72', 'ac': '2,200 W (4,400 W surge)', 'price': '$1,239 (maker, 2026-11-13)'}}, {'slug': 'bluetti-elite-200-v2-200w-solar-kit', 'model': 'BLUETTI Elite 200 V2 + 200 W', 'cells': {'usable': '1,910 Wh (StorageReview)', 'battery': '2,073.6 Wh', 'panels': '1 × 200 W (SP200L)', 'per_wh': '$0.63', 'ac': '2,600 W'}}, {'slug': 'bluetti-ac180-200w-solar-kit', 'model': 'BLUETTI AC180 + 200 W', 'cells': {'usable': '950 Wh (OutdoorGearLab)', 'battery': '1,152 Wh', 'panels': '1 × 200 W', 'per_wh': '$0.81', 'ac': '1,800 W (2,700 W Power Lifting mode)'}}, {'brand': 'EcoFlow', 'model': 'DELTA 3 Solar Generator (DELTA 3 + 220 W panel)', 'url': 'https://us.ecoflow.com/products/ecoflow-delta-3-solar-generator', 'cells': {'usable': '870 Wh (OutdoorGearLab)', 'battery': '1,024 Wh', 'panels': '1 × 220 W', 'per_wh': '$0.84', 'ac': '1,800 W', 'price': '$729 (maker, 2026-11-13)'}}, {'slug': 'bluetti-ac180-2x200w-solar-kit', 'model': 'BLUETTI AC180 + 2 × 200 W', 'cells': {'usable': '950 Wh (OutdoorGearLab)', 'battery': '1,152 Wh', 'panels': '2 × 200 W', 'per_wh': '$1.30', 'ac': '1,800 W (2,700 W Power Lifting mode)'}}],
 "after": "\n<h2>What the differences mean</h2><p><strong>Usable share of the rated battery.</strong> Elite 200 V2: 1,910 ÷ 2,073.6 = 92% (StorageReview). Explorer 2000 v2: 1,710 ÷ 2,042 = 84%. DELTA 3: 870 ÷ 1,024 = 85%. AC180: 950 ÷ 1,152 = 82% (all three OutdoorGearLab, measured at the AC outlets). StorageReview doesn't say whether its discharge ran through the AC outlets. Even if it lost the same 15% as OutdoorGearLab's AC tests, the Elite 200 V2 would deliver 2,073.6 × 0.85 = 1,763 Wh. That is still the most of any kit here.</p><p><strong>Price per usable Wh.</strong> Elite 200 V2 + 2 × 200 W: 1,499 ÷ 1,910 = $0.78. Jackery Solar Generator 2000 v2: 1,239 ÷ 1,710 = $0.72. Elite 200 V2 + 200 W: 1,199 ÷ 1,910 = $0.63. AC180 + 200 W: 769 ÷ 950 = $0.81. DELTA 3 + 220 W: 729 ÷ 870 = $0.84. AC180 + 2 × 200 W: 1,232 ÷ 950 = $1.30. The Jackery costs less per usable Wh, but Jackery's store lists it as sold out and on pre-order, shipping Nov 16. BLUETTI's store takes orders for the Elite 200 V2 kits now but says their 200 W panels ship from Nov 18.</p><p><strong>Hours of full sun to refill at the panels' rated watts.</strong> Elite 200 V2 + 2 × 200 W: 2,073.6 ÷ 400 = 5.2 h. Elite 200 V2 + 200 W: 2,073.6 ÷ 200 = 10.4 h. Jackery 2000 v2: 2,042 ÷ 400 = 5.1 h. AC180 + 200 W: 1,152 ÷ 200 = 5.8 h. DELTA 3 + 220 W: 1,024 ÷ 220 = 4.7 h. AC180 + 2 × 200 W: 1,152 ÷ 400 = 2.9 h. These figures don't count charging losses, and losses are real: StorageReview's wall recharge of the Elite 200 V2 drew 2,440 Wh, which is 2,440 ÷ 2,073.6 = 18% more than the rated battery. Expect solar refills to take longer than the figures above.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Use</th><th>Kit</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Fridge and essentials through an outage, refilled by sun</td><td>Elite 200 V2 + 2 × 200 W</td><td>1,910 Wh measured, 2,600 W inverter, 400 W of panels, 1,000 W solar input for adding more later</td></tr><tr><td>Lowest cost for 2 kWh with 400 W of panels</td><td>Jackery Solar Generator 2000 v2</td><td>$0.72 per usable Wh; pre-order, ships Nov 16</td></tr><tr><td>Most stored energy per dollar, charged mostly from the wall or a generator</td><td>Elite 200 V2 + 200 W</td><td>$0.63 per usable Wh, but one panel needs 10.4 h of full sun</td></tr><tr><td>Camping, laptops, CPAP, short outages</td><td>AC180 + 200 W or DELTA 3 + 220 W</td><td>950 Wh and 870 Wh measured; both 1,800 W</td></tr><tr><td>Loads above 2,600 W</td><td>Jackery HomePower 3000</td><td>Jackery rates it at 3,600 W continuous (7,200 W surge)</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Buy the pick: {buy:bluetti-elite-200-v2-2x200w-solar-kit}. Cheapest per usable Wh: {buy:bluetti-elite-200-v2-200w-solar-kit}. 1 kWh starter: {buy:bluetti-ac180-200w-solar-kit}.</p><h2>What the panels in the box actually measured</h2><p>OutdoorGearLab (Sam Schild, updated 2026-07-13) used each panel to charge the same 1,070 Wh Jackery 1000 for two hours on a clear day at 6,300 ft and 55–65°F, logging input every 30 minutes. Results were: EcoFlow NextGen 220W, 193 W of 220 W (88%); Jackery SolarSaga 200, 171 W of 200 W (86%); Anker SOLIX PS200, 166 W of 200 W (83%); Bluetti 200W Portable, 150 W of 200 W (75%).</p><p>Read those numbers against the panel your kit actually ships. The Bluetti panel OutdoorGearLab tested weighed 18.9 lb and folds to 23.9 × 23.9 in. That doesn't match the 17.15 lb SP200L that BLUETTI's Elite 200 V2 kit listings point to (their store addresses end in sp200l), so the 150 W result says nothing about the SP200L. Before you count on 193 W from an EcoFlow kit, check that the listing names the NextGen 220W. For Jackery, the SolarSaga 200 result applies directly. Two of them at 171 W each make 342 W, so 2,042 ÷ 342 = 6.0 h of full sun for the 2000 v2.</p><p><strong>Anker SOLIX C1000 Gen 2 + PS200 bifacial.</strong> OutdoorGearLab measured 890 Wh of usable energy from the 1,024 Wh station (87%). Anker lists the solar input as 11–28 V at 8.2 A and 29–60 V at 14.5 A, with a 600 W maximum. The bundled PS200 bifacial is a 48 V, 4.16 A panel, so it charges in the full-current band. A typical 18–20 V panel would fall into the 8.2 A band and top out around 8.2 × 20 = 164 W. Two PS200s in series reach 96 V, which is over the 60 V limit, so any added panels must go in parallel. Three in parallel come to 3 × 4.16 = 12.5 A, about 599 W.</p><h2>Not recommended</h2><p><strong>BLUETTI AC180 + 2 × 200 W at $1,232.</strong> On BLUETTI's own store the Elite 200 V2 + 2 × 200 W costs $267 more ($1,499) for the same 400 W of panels and roughly twice the energy: 1,910 Wh measured against 950 Wh, and 2,073.6 Wh rated against 1,152 Wh. The two panels also cost more than the battery they charge: the AC180 alone is $499, so the panels add 1,232 − 499 = $733. If you want an AC180, the single-panel $769 kit is the one that makes sense.</p>\n",
 "sources": [('Elite 200 V2: 1.91 kWh discharged, 2.44 kWh to recharge, 2,073.6 Wh rated, 2,600 W inverter, 1,000 W / 12–60 V solar input, 53.4 lb (StorageReview, read 2026-11-13)', 'https://www.storagereview.com/review/portable-power-meets-lab-grade-reliability-bluetti-elite-200-v2-review'), ('BLUETTI Elite 200 V2 + 200 W kit price $1,199, orderable; 200 W panel ships from Nov 18 (read 2026-11-13)', 'https://www.bluettipower.com/products/elite-200-v2-sp200l'), ('BLUETTI Elite 200 V2 + 2 × 200 W kit price $1,499, orderable; 200 W panel ships from Nov 18; 2,600 W continuous AC, 1,000 W solar input (read 2026-11-13)', 'https://www.bluettipower.com/products/elite-200-v2-2-sp200l'), ('BLUETTI AC180 station $499, + 200 W $769, + 2 × 200 W $1,232; 1,800 W AC / 2,700 W Power Lifting mode; 1,152 Wh (read 2026-11-13)', 'https://www.bluettipower.com/products/ac180'), ('BLUETTI SP200L 200 W panel weight 17.15 lb (read 2026-11-13)', 'https://www.bluettipower.com/products/bluetti-sp200l-solar-panel-200w'), ('Measured panel output: EcoFlow NextGen 220W 193 W, Jackery SolarSaga 200 171 W, Anker PS200 166 W, Bluetti 200W 150 W; test method (OutdoorGearLab, read 2026-11-13)', 'https://www.outdoorgearlab.com/topics/camping-and-hiking/best-portable-solar-panel'), ('The Bluetti 200W panel OutdoorGearLab tested: 18.9 lb, 23.9 × 23.9 in folded (OutdoorGearLab, read 2026-11-13)', 'https://www.outdoorgearlab.com/reviews/camping-and-hiking/portable-solar-panel/bluetti-200w-portable'), ('Measured usable AC output: Explorer 2000 v2 1,710 Wh, DELTA 3 870 Wh, C1000 Gen 2 890 Wh (OutdoorGearLab, read 2026-11-13)', 'https://www.outdoorgearlab.com/topics/camping-and-hiking/best-power-station'), ('BLUETTI AC180 measured usable output 950 Wh (OutdoorGearLab, read 2026-11-13)', 'https://www.outdoorgearlab.com/reviews/camping-and-hiking/power-station/bluetti-ac180'), ('Jackery Solar Generator 2000 v2: $1,239, sold out with pre-order shipping Nov 16; 2,042 Wh; 2,200 W continuous, 4,400 W surge (read 2026-11-13)', 'https://www.jackery.com/products/jackery-solar-generator-2000-v2'), ('EcoFlow DELTA 3 Solar Generator: $729; 1,800 W AC output (read 2026-11-13)', 'https://us.ecoflow.com/products/ecoflow-delta-3-solar-generator'), ('Anker SOLIX C1000 Gen 2 solar input 11–28 V at 8.2 A and 29–60 V at 14.5 A, 600 W max; 2,000 W continuous (read 2026-11-13)', 'https://www.ankersolix.com/products/c1000-gen2?variant=61869573308746'), ('Anker SOLIX PS200 bifacial PV output 48 V, 4.16 A (read 2026-11-13)', 'https://www.ankersolix.com/products/ps200-bifacial-portable-solar-panel'), ('Jackery HomePower 3000: 3,600 W continuous, 7,200 W surge (read 2026-11-13)', 'https://www.jackery.com/products/jackery-solar-generator-homepower-3000')],
 "published": '2026-10-25',
 "checked": '2026-11-14',
 "updated": '2026-11-14'},

