{"slug": 'best-power-bank-for-steam-deck',
 "question": 'G07 (FC41 funnel: Steam Deck / handheld)',
 "method": 'ab-2026-11', "all_links": True,
 "angle": 'E',
 "searched_as": ['Steam Deck official power supply 45W battery capacity OLED LCD USB C PD power bank', 'best power bank Steam Deck 2026 45W USB C Anker UGREEN Baseus comparison', 'best Steam Deck power bank 2026 45W USB C PD Anker Ugreen INIU reviews', 'best Steam Deck power bank 2026 Anker UGREEN Baseus 45W USB C PD Steam Deck battery', 'best power banks Steam Deck OLED 2026 Anker Prime INIU Baseus USB C PD 45W', 'Steam Deck OLED LCD battery capacity 50Wh 40Wh charging 45W Valve official;best power bank Steam Deck Anker Ugreen Baseus 2026'],
 "title": 'Best power bank for Steam Deck (2026): 45W USB-C PD, capacity and airline limits compared',
 "h1": 'Best power bank for Steam Deck (2026): 45W USB-C PD and airline limits',
 "desc": 'Steam Deck power banks ranked by measured delivered energy (Techtest.org), converted to extra Deck OLED play hours at a 24 W load, with the 15V/3A port check and the 100 Wh airline limit. Maker prices checked 2026-11-13.',
 "answer": '<p class="lead"><strong>Short answer.</strong> The best power bank for Steam Deck is the UGREEN Nexode 25,000mAh 165W: Techtest measured 72.6 Wh delivered, about 3 hours of extra Steam Deck OLED play at a 24 W full load, and every USB-C output offers the 15V/3A level the Deck\'s 45W USB-C PD charging uses.</p>',
 "columns": [('energy', 'Delivered energy (Techtest.org)'), ('hours', 'Extra Deck OLED play at 24 W'), ('charges', 'Full Deck OLED charges (50 Wh)'), ('port15', 'USB-C outputs with 15V⎓3A')],
 "rows": [{'slug': 'ugreen-nexode-25000mah-165w-built-in-cables', 'model': 'UGREEN Nexode Power Bank 25,000 mAh 165W with Built-in Cables (PB552)', 'cells': {'energy': '72.6 Wh average (65.2–76.8 Wh by load)', 'hours': 'about 3.0 h (2.7–3.2 h)', 'charges': 'about 1.45', 'port15': 'All three: 140 W cable, 65 W cable, 65 W port (Techtest)'}}, {'brand': 'Anker', 'model': 'Laptop Power Bank 25K 165W, Built-In and Retractable Cables (A1695)', 'url': 'https://www.anker.com/products/a1695-anker-power-bank-25000mah-165w', 'cells': {'energy': '74.2 Wh average (70.3–78.4 Wh by load)', 'hours': 'about 3.1 h (2.9–3.3 h)', 'charges': 'about 1.48', 'port15': 'Every USB-C port and cable (Anker)', 'price': '$119.99 (maker, 2026-11-13)'}}, {'brand': 'Anker', 'model': 'Prime Power Bank 26K 300W (A110A)', 'url': 'https://www.anker.com/products/a110a-anker-prime-26k-300w-power-bank', 'cells': {'energy': '79.6–89.8 Wh', 'hours': 'about 3.3–3.7 h', 'charges': 'about 1.6–1.8', 'port15': 'Listed on its USB-C output line, 140 W max (Anker)', 'price': '$229.99 (maker, 2026-11-13)'}}, {'brand': 'UGREEN', 'model': 'Nexode Power Bank 20,000 mAh 165W with Retractable USB-C Cable (PB726)', 'url': 'https://us.ugreen.com/products/ugreen-retractable-cable-power-bank-20000mah', 'cells': {'energy': '64.9 Wh average (62.5–66.4 Wh by load)', 'hours': 'about 2.7 h (2.6–2.8 h)', 'charges': 'about 1.3', 'port15': 'USB-C port (Techtest)', 'price': '$99.99 (maker, 2026-11-13)'}}, {'brand': 'UGREEN', 'model': 'Nexode Power Bank 20,000 mAh 130W with Smart Digital Display', 'url': 'https://us.ugreen.com/products/ugreen-nexode-power-bank-20000mah-130w', 'cells': {'energy': '60.7 Wh average (54.8–64.7 Wh, falling as load rises)', 'hours': 'about 2.5 h (2.3–2.7 h)', 'charges': 'about 1.2', 'port15': 'USB-C1 only; USB-C2 tops out at 12V⎓2.5A, 30 W (UGREEN)', 'price': '$89.99 (maker, 2026-11-13)'}}],
 "after": '\n<h2>What the differences mean</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Extra play time</strong> = delivered Wh ÷ 24 W (Steam Deck OLED at full load). UGREEN 25K: 72.6 ÷ 24 = 3.0 h. Anker A1695: 74.2 ÷ 24 = 3.1 h. Anker Prime 26K: 79.6–89.8 ÷ 24 = 3.3–3.7 h. UGREEN 20K 165W: 64.9 ÷ 24 = 2.7 h. UGREEN 20K 130W: 60.7 ÷ 24 = 2.5 h. The Deck loses some energy charging its own battery, so real sessions run a little shorter. Light games draw far less, so the hours stretch.</li>\n<li><strong>Full OLED charges</strong> = delivered Wh ÷ 50 Wh. 72.6 ÷ 50 = 1.45; 74.2 ÷ 50 = 1.48; 79.6–89.8 ÷ 50 = 1.6–1.8; 64.9 ÷ 50 = 1.3; 60.7 ÷ 50 = 1.2. No bank under the 100 Wh airline line gets to two full charges.</li>\n<li><strong>Cost per measured Wh</strong> = price ÷ delivered Wh. UGREEN 25K: 109.99 ÷ 72.6 = $1.52. Anker A1695: 119.99 ÷ 74.2 = $1.62. Anker Prime 26K: 229.99 ÷ 89.8–79.6 = $2.56–2.89. UGREEN 20K 165W: 99.99 ÷ 64.9 = $1.54. UGREEN 20K 130W: 89.99 ÷ 60.7 = $1.48.</li>\n<li><strong>The step up to Anker</strong>: the A1695 costs $10 more than the UGREEN 25K and delivers 1.6 Wh more (74.2 − 72.6), about 4 minutes at 24 W. The Prime 26K costs $120 more and delivers 7.0–17.2 Wh more, 18–43 minutes.</li>\n<li><strong>The step down to 20,000 mAh</strong>: the UGREEN 20K 130W saves $20 but delivers 11.9 Wh less (72.6 − 60.7), about 30 minutes less play at 24 W.</li>\n</ul>\n<table>\n<thead><tr><th>Use</th><th>Fits</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>Deck plus a phone or tablet from one bag</td><td>UGREEN Nexode 25,000 mAh 165W {buy:ugreen-nexode-25000mah-165w-built-in-cables}</td><td>Two built-in cables and a port, all with 15V⎓3A, so either cable charges the Deck at full rate</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Longest sessions while staying under 100 Wh</td><td>Anker Prime 26K 300W</td><td>79.6–89.8 Wh measured; Anker labels it 99.75 Wh</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Lightest bank with more than one full charge</td><td>UGREEN Nexode 20,000 mAh 130W</td><td>475 g (Techtest), 60.7 Wh measured, 15V⎓3A on USB-C1 only</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Lowest price in the measured set</td><td>UGREEN Nexode 20,000 mAh 130W</td><td>$1.48 per measured Wh, but plug the Deck into USB-C1 only</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2>Measured, not estimated: what the tests show</h2>\n<p><strong>Delivered energy.</strong> Techtest.org (Michael Barton) drains each bank through an electronic load at fixed voltages and logs the energy that comes out. The UGREEN 25K gave 65.2 Wh at 5 V/1 A, 71.9 Wh at 9 V/1 A, 75.0 Wh at 9 V/3 A, 76.8 Wh at 20 V/1 A and 74.1 Wh at 20 V/3 A, averaging 72.6 Wh (78% of its 25,000 mAh rating). The Anker A1695 averaged 74.2 Wh. The UGREEN 20K 130W did worst under load: it dropped from 64.7 Wh at 9 V/3 A to 54.8 Wh at 20 V/5 A.</p>\n<p><strong>Heat throttling.</strong> Techtest found the UGREEN 25K holds 140 W for about half its capacity, then falls to 65 W until it cools. The 20K 165W drops to 65 W for its last 20%. Both floors are above the Deck\'s 45 W, so neither limits a Deck.</p>\n<p><strong>Why the 15V⎓3A line matters more than total watts.</strong> ChargerLAB measured the Steam Deck triggering the 15 V PD level and drawing about 39 W from Valve\'s own 45 W adapter. Level1Techs staff (<a href="https://forum.level1techs.com/t/usb-c-kvm-switch-v3-with-usb-power-delivery-135watts-does-not-fast-charge-steamdeck-stuck-in-15w-mode/253306">forum thread</a>) report that a source offering 20 V but no 15 V drops the Deck to 5 V / 15 W. A 165 W or 300 W total adds no speed; what matters is 15V⎓3A on the port you plug into. On the UGREEN 20K 130W that is USB-C1 only.</p>\n<p><strong>How hard the Deck pulls.</strong> The Phawx measured the Steam Deck OLED at 24 W total system power in Cyberpunk 2077, as reported by Notebookcheck. Valve rates the OLED at 50 Wh and 3–12 hours of play, which works out to 4.2–16.7 W average.</p>\n<p><strong>Airline limits.</strong> Under FAA rules, as AARP reports them, power banks up to 100 Wh need no approval, 101–160 Wh need the airline\'s approval (two spares at most), and any power bank must travel in carry-on bags only. Anker labels the Prime 26K at 99.75 Wh and the A1695 at 90 Wh. For the 25,000 mAh UGREEN, 25,000 mAh × 3.6–3.7 V = 90–92.5 Wh, under the 100 Wh line. Check the Wh printed on the label before you fly.</p>\n<h2>Not recommended</h2>\n<p><strong>INIU Carry 20,000 mAh 45W (P51L-E2)</strong>, $36.99 at <a href="https://iniushop.com/products/iniu-p51l-e2-power-bank-45w-20000mah">INIU</a> (2026-11-13). It lists 15V⎓3A, but Techtest measured it throttling from 45 W to about 27 W under sustained load from heat, and down to 17 W while charging a laptop. Against the Deck OLED\'s measured 24 W in heavy games, that leaves about 3 W to charge the Deck while you play. It is fine for topping up between sessions, not for playing while it charges.</p>\n',
 "sources": [('UGREEN Nexode 25,000 mAh 165W (PB552): delivered Wh by load, throttling, 15V⎓3A on all USB-C outputs, 545 g (Techtest.org, read 2026-11-13)', 'https://techtest.org/ugreen-nexode-power-bank-25000-mah-165w-im-test-viel-leistung-zum-fairen-preis/'), ('UGREEN Nexode 25,000 mAh 165W with Built-in Cables price $109.99 (UGREEN US, read 2026-11-13)', 'https://us.ugreen.com/products/nexode-power-bank-25000mah-165w-built-in-cables'), ('Anker A1695 delivered Wh by load (Techtest.org, read 2026-11-13)', 'https://techtest.org/anker-zolo-power-bank-25-000-mah-165-w-im-test-leistungsstarke-powerbank-mit-dual-usb-c-kabel/'), ('Anker A1695 price $119.99, 15V⎓3A on each USB-C, 90 Wh, 595 g (Anker US, read 2026-11-13)', 'https://www.anker.com/products/a1695-anker-power-bank-25000mah-165w'), ('Anker Prime 26K delivered 79.6–89.8 Wh (Techtest.org, read 2026-11-13)', 'https://techtest.org/die-anker-prime-26k-300w-powerbank-im-test-der-neue-gold-standard/'), ('Anker Prime 26K price $229.99, 99.75 Wh, 15V⎓3A, 600 g, Steam Deck listed (Anker US, read 2026-11-13)', 'https://www.anker.com/products/a110a-anker-prime-26k-300w-power-bank'), ('UGREEN 20K 165W Retractable (PB726): delivered Wh, 65 W fallback, 15V⎓3A on the USB-C port, 538 g (Techtest.org, read 2026-11-13)', 'https://techtest.org/ugreen-nexode-20000mah-powerbank-test-165w-mit-retractable-cable/'), ('UGREEN 20K 130W delivered Wh by load (Techtest.org, read 2026-11-13)', 'https://techtest.org/ugreen-nexode-130w-20000mah-powerbank-im-test-leistung-kapazitaet-und-ladezeit-im-ueberblick'), ('UGREEN 20K 130W per-port profiles (USB-C2 30 W max, no 15 V) and price $89.99 (UGREEN US, read 2026-11-13)', 'https://us.ugreen.com/products/ugreen-nexode-power-bank-20000mah-130w'), ('Steam Deck OLED 24 W full-load draw measured by The Phawx (Notebookcheck, read 2026-11-13)', 'https://www.notebookcheck.net/Steam-Deck-OLED-leads-at-24-W-but-Switch-2-delivers-2-5x-more-FPS-at-8-6-W-TDP-in-the-latest-detailed-comparison.1052877.0.html'), ('Steam Deck OLED 50 Wh battery, 3–12 h play, 45 W supply (Valve, read 2026-11-13)', 'https://www.steamdeck.com/en/oled'), ("Steam Deck triggers the 15 V PD level, about 39 W from Valve's adapter (ChargerLAB, read 2026-11-13)", 'https://chargerlab.com/exploring-the-charging-detail-of-your-steam-deck-chargerlab-compatibility-100'), ('INIU Carry 45W (P51L-E2) throttles to about 27 W sustained, 15V⎓3A listed (Techtest.org, read 2026-11-13)', 'https://techtest.org/iniu-p51l-e2-45w-20-000-mah-im-test-kompakt-stark-aber-temperatur-gedrosselt/'), ('FAA power bank limits: 100 Wh, 101–160 Wh with airline approval, carry-on only (AARP, Edward C. Baig, read 2026-11-13)', 'https://www.aarp.org/personal-technology/portable-charger-on-a-plane/')],
 "published": '2026-11-02',
 "checked": '2026-11-14',
 "updated": '2026-11-14'},

