{"slug": 'best-65w-travel-charger-interchangeable-plugs',
 "question": 'G20 (UGREEN funnel: 65W travel charger with US/UK/EU plugs)',
 "method": 'ab-2026-11', "all_links": True,
 "angle": 'D',
 "searched_as": ['best 65W USB C travel charger interchangeable US UK EU plug heads 2026 reviews', 'best 65W GaN travel charger interchangeable US UK EU plugs 2026 reviews', 'best 65W USB C GaN charger interchangeable US UK EU plug heads 2026', 'best 65W GaN charger interchangeable US UK EU plug adapters 2026', 'best 65W USB C GaN travel charger interchangeable US UK EU plug adapters 2026', 'best 65W USB C GaN charger interchangeable US UK EU plug attachments 2026'],
 "title": 'Best 65W travel charger with interchangeable US, UK and EU plugs (2026)',
 "h1": 'Best 65W travel charger with interchangeable US, UK and EU plugs (2026)',
 "desc": 'Which 65W GaN travel charger with swappable US, UK and EU plug heads to buy, and why your USB-C cable decides whether the laptop gets 65 W or 60 W. Prices checked 13 Nov 2026.',
 "answer": '<p class="lead"><strong>Short answer.</strong> The best 65W travel charger with interchangeable US, UK and EU plugs is the UGREEN Nexode 65W 3-port GaN charger (2 USB-C + USB-A, swappable plug heads). For the full 65W into a laptop, use a 5 A USB-C cable: an ordinary 3 A cable caps it at 60W (20 V × 3 A).</p>',
 "columns": [('plugs', 'Plug heads'), ('ports', 'Ports'), ('laptop_w', 'Laptop port rating'), ('cable3a', 'Laptop max on a 3 A cable')],
 "rows": [{'slug': 'ugreen-nexode-65w-travel-charger-us-uk-eu', 'model': 'UGREEN Nexode 65W 3-Port Travel Charger (90409)', 'cells': {'plugs': 'Foldable US prongs + switchable UK and EU heads (UGREEN)', 'ports': '2× USB-C + USB-A', 'laptop_w': '65 W on USB-C (UGREEN)', 'cable3a': '60 W'}}, {'brand': 'Native Union', 'model': 'International Fast GaN Charger PD 67W (3 ports)', 'url': 'https://www.nativeunion.com/products/fast-gan-charger-pd-67w-3ports', 'cells': {'plugs': 'US/CA, EU and UK adapters (Native Union)', 'ports': '2× USB-C + USB-A', 'laptop_w': '67 W on USB-C (Native Union)', 'cable3a': '60 W', 'price': '$59.99 (maker, 2026-11-13)'}}, {'brand': 'KUXIU', 'model': '65W UltraSlim GaN Adapter, US plug + EU & UK adapter set', 'url': 'https://kuxiu.com/products/kuxiu-65w-adapter', 'cells': {'plugs': 'US prongs + snap-on EU and UK adapters (KUXIU)', 'ports': '2× USB-C', 'laptop_w': '65 W total (KUXIU)', 'cable3a': '60 W at most', 'price': '$28.99 (maker, 2026-11-13)'}}, {'slug': 'tessan-gan-65w-universal-travel-adapter-wta07', 'model': 'TESSAN GaN 65W Universal Travel Adapter (WTA07)', 'cells': {'plugs': 'Sliding US, UK, EU and AU pins (universal adapter, TESSAN)', 'ports': '3× USB-C + 2× USB-A', 'laptop_w': '65 W on USB-C3 only; other USB ports 15 W max each (TESSAN)', 'cable3a': '60 W'}}, {'brand': 'Native Union', 'model': 'Fast GaN Charger PD 67W (2 ports)', 'url': 'https://www.nativeunion.com/products/fast-gan-charger-pd-67w', 'cells': {'plugs': 'US/CA, EU and UK adapters (Native Union)', 'ports': '2× USB-C', 'laptop_w': '67 W on USB-C (Native Union)', 'cable3a': '60 W', 'price': '$59.99 (maker, 2026-11-13)'}}],
 "after": '\n<h2>What the differences mean</h2><p><strong>On a 3 A cable, all five chargers stop at 60 W.</strong> 20 V × 3 A = 60 W. A 65 W rating needs 65 ÷ 20 = 3.25 A, and 67 W needs 67 ÷ 20 = 3.35 A. Both are above 3 A. On a basic cable, Native Union\'s extra 2 W makes no difference.</p><p><strong>With a phone also plugged in, the laptop gets 45 W on every split we could source.</strong> Best Batteries gives the UGREEN as 45 W + 20 W (45 ÷ 65 = 69% of the rating to the laptop). Verbatim lists its 32201 at 45 W + 18 W, and D-Link lists its DCP-651 at 45 W + 20 W. At 45 W the laptop draws 45 ÷ 20 = 2.25 A, which any 3 A cable carries. So the cable only matters when the laptop is charging on its own.</p><p><strong>Price.</strong> Native Union\'s 3-port costs $59.99 − $44.98 = $15.01 more than the UGREEN, for 2 W more rating and the same 2 USB-C + USB-A layout. KUXIU costs $44.98 − $28.99 = $15.99 less but has no USB-A port.</p><table><tr><th>Your trip</th><th>Fits best</th></tr><tr><td>Laptop, phone and earbuds in the US, UK and Europe</td><td>UGREEN Nexode 65W travel charger</td></tr><tr><td>Only two USB-C devices and the smallest bag kit, for Europe and the UK</td><td>KUXIU 65W UltraSlim</td></tr><tr><td>Australia too, or five USB devices from one wall socket</td><td>TESSAN WTA07 (only USB-C3 reaches 65 W)</td></tr><tr><td>A stated 2-year warranty and a MacBook Pro 14"</td><td>Native Union 67W, 3-port</td></tr></table><h2>The cable decides whether you get 65 W or 60 W</h2><p>USB-C chargers reach 65 W at 20 V and 3.25 A. TI\'s engineers Brian Gosselin and Nate Enos explain that USB-C cables "are required to be electronically marked if they are either full-featured and/or rated at more than 3A current", and that "electronically marked cables use USB PD to provide the cable\'s characteristics". A cable without that chip is treated as a 3 A cable, so the charger offers at most 20 V × 3 A = 60 W.</p><p>UGREEN\'s own specs show the same limit. On its Nexode 65W charger with a retractable cable, UGREEN rates the built-in cable at "20V/3A 60W Max" and the separate USB-C port beside it at "20V/3.25A 65W Max". The travel charger does not come with a USB-C cable (SmartGadgetKit and Best Batteries), so the cable you pack sets the ceiling. Best Batteries says about 62 W reaches a laptop from the UGREEN on one port, which is more than the 60 W a 3 A cable can carry at 20 V.</p><p><strong>What to pack.</strong> Get the {buy:ugreen-nexode-65w-travel-charger-us-uk-eu} and a cable rated 100 W. A 100 W rating at 20 V means 100 ÷ 20 = 5 A, so the cable is e-marked. Baseus\'s 100 W USB-C cable is $9.99 on its own store {buy:baseus-usb-c-cable-100w}. Plug the laptop into the first USB-C port. On the two chargers whose makers publish every port pairing, Verbatim\'s 32201 and D-Link\'s DCP-651, the second USB-C port and the USB-A port together share just 15 W.</p>\n',
 "sources": [('UGREEN Nexode 65W 3-Port Travel Charger price $44.98 (was $61.43), UGREEN US store, read 2026-11-13', 'https://us.ugreen.com/products/ugreen-65w-nexode-gan-usb-c-3-port-charger-with-us-uk-eu-plug-for-travel'), ('UGREEN: US/UK/EU plugs included, foldable US plug, switchable plug, max 65 W from the USB-C port (UGREEN UK, read 2026-11-13)', 'https://uk.ugreen.com/products/ugreen-nexode-65w-gan-travel-charger-3-ports'), ('UGREEN 45 W + 20 W split, about 62 W reaching a laptop, 91.6% efficiency, no cable in the box (Best Batteries, read 2026-11-13)', 'https://en.best-batteries.com/reviews/ugreen-nexode-65w-charger/'), ('UGREEN plug heads release with a button; no USB-C cable in the box (SmartGadgetKit, read 2026-11-13)', 'https://smartgadgetkit.com/ugreen-nexode-65w-travel-charger-review/'), ('USB-C cables rated above 3 A must be electronically marked and report their limits over USB PD (TI, Gosselin and Enos, read 2026-11-13)', 'https://ti.com/document-viewer/lit/html/SSZTBJ8/GUID-61351F5F-3B46-4F6A-A613-320B3A36C17A'), ('UGREEN Nexode 65W retractable-cable charger: built-in cable 20V/3A 60 W max, USB-C port 20V/3.25A 65 W max (UGREEN EU, read 2026-11-13)', 'https://eu.ugreen.com/products/nexode-65w-charger-retractable-cable'), ('Native Union 67W 3-port: $59.99, 2 USB-C + 1 USB-A, US/CA, EU and UK adapters, 2-year limited warranty (read 2026-11-13)', 'https://www.nativeunion.com/products/fast-gan-charger-pd-67w-3ports'), ('Native Union 67W 2-port: $59.99, 2 USB-C, US/CA, EU and UK adapters (read 2026-11-13)', 'https://www.nativeunion.com/products/fast-gan-charger-pd-67w'), ('KUXIU 65W UltraSlim: $28.99, two USB-C ports, snap-on EU and UK adapters (read 2026-11-13)', 'https://kuxiu.com/products/kuxiu-65w-adapter'), ('TESSAN WTA07: $42.99, 65 W from USB-C3 only, other USB ports 15 W max each, sliding US/UK/EU/AU pins (read 2026-11-13)', 'https://www.tessan.com/products/gan-65w-universal-travel-adapter-wta07'), ('Verbatim 32201: 20V 3.25A per USB-C port, C1 + C2 45 W + 18 W, C2 + USB-A 15 W combined (Verbatim, read 2026-11-13)', 'https://www.verbatim-europe.com/en/wall-chargers/products/65w-3-port-gan-wall-charger-2-x-usb-c-pd-65w-1-x-usb-a-qc-30-euukus-32201'), ('D-Link DCP-651: C1 + C2 45 W + 20 W, C2 + A 15 W total (D-Link, read 2026-11-13)', 'https://www.dlink.com/pl/pl/products/dcp-651-65w-gan-charger'), ("Baseus USB-C to USB-C cable 100 W, $9.99 on Baseus's store (read 2026-11-13)", 'https://www.baseus.com/products/usb-c-to-usb-c-cable-100w')],
 "published": '2026-11-03',
 "checked": '2026-11-14',
 "updated": '2026-11-14'},

# ---------------- best-nas-under-500-for-docker-immich-home-assistant (research method ab-2026-11, 2026-11-08) ----------------
{"slug": 'best-nas-under-500-for-docker-immich-home-assistant',
 "question": 'G21 (UGREEN funnel: NAS under $500 for Docker, Immich, Home Assistant)',
 "method": 'ab-2026-11', "all_links": True,
 "angle": 'B',
 "searched_as": ['2026 UGREEN DXP2800 TerraMaster F2-424 Beelink ME Mini price docker immich home assistant NAS review', '2026 best NAS under $500 Docker Immich Home Assistant UGREEN DXP2800 TerraMaster F2-424 prices specs', '2026 best NAS under $500 Intel N100 Docker Immich Home Assistant UGREEN DXP2800 TerraMaster F4-424 prices'],
 "title": 'Best NAS under $500 for Docker containers like Immich and Home Assistant (2026)',
 "h1": 'Best NAS under $500 for Docker, Immich and Home Assistant (2026)',
 "desc": 'RAM left for Docker after Immich and a Home Assistant OS VM, enclosure by enclosure: UGREEN DXP2800 vs TerraMaster F2-425 Plus, F2-425, Synology DS225+.',
 "answer": '<p class="lead"><strong>Short answer.</strong> The best NAS under $500 for Docker containers like Immich and Home Assistant is the UGREEN NASync DXP2800: Intel N100, 8 GB stock, $389.99 at UGREEN. Upgraded to 16 GB it leaves 6 GB free after Immich\'s 8 GB and a 2 GB Home Assistant OS VM.</p>',
 "columns": [('cpu', 'CPU'), ('ram', 'RAM shipped (maker maximum)'), ('headroom', 'RAM left after Immich + Home Assistant OS VM'), ('lan', 'LAN')],
 "rows": [{'slug': 'ugreen-nasync-dxp2800', 'model': 'UGREEN NASync DXP2800', 'cells': {'cpu': 'Intel N100, 4 cores, Quick Sync', 'ram': "8 GB DDR5, one SO-DIMM slot; 16 GB maximum (UGREEN, via The Gadgeteer), the same as Intel's N100 ceiling", 'headroom': '0 GB at stock 8 GB with Immich at its 6 GB minimum; 6 GB at 16 GB with Immich at its 8 GB recommendation. UGOS Pro Virtual Machine app runs Home Assistant OS', 'lan': '1× 2.5GbE'}}, {"asin": 'B0GW85XHRP', 'brand': 'TerraMaster', 'model': 'F2-425 Plus', 'url': 'https://www.terra-master.com/products/f2-425-plus', 'cells': {'price': '$399.49 (maker, 2026-11-08)', 'cpu': 'Intel N150, 4 cores (ITPro, Dave Mitchell)', 'ram': '8 GB DDR5, one SO-DIMM slot; 32 GB maximum per TerraMaster (ITPro). Intel rates the N150 at 16 GB', 'headroom': "0 GB at stock 8 GB; 22 GB at 32 GB, or 6 GB at Intel's 16 GB rating. Three M.2 NVMe slots for the Immich database", 'lan': '2× 5GbE'}}, {"asin": 'B0FHVZ53RN', 'brand': 'TerraMaster', 'model': 'F2-425', 'url': 'https://www.terra-master.com/products/f2-425', 'cells': {'price': '$299.99 (maker, 2026-11-08)', 'cpu': 'Intel x86 quad-core (TerraMaster store listing)', 'ram': '4 GB (TerraMaster store listing)', 'headroom': "−4 GB: 4 GB is below Immich's 6 GB minimum, so Immich runs only with machine learning disabled and nothing is left for a Home Assistant OS VM", 'lan': '1× 2.5GbE'}}],
 "after": "\n<h2>What the differences mean</h2>\n<p>Immich's own requirements page asks for 6 GB of RAM minimum and 8 GB recommended, and says a 4 GB machine can run it only with machine learning disabled. Home Assistant's installation page says a Container (Docker) install has no Apps, the add-on store, and no out-of-the-box Thread or Z-Wave. To get full Home Assistant on a NAS you run Home Assistant OS as a virtual machine, which Home Assistant specifies at 2 GB of RAM, 2 vCPUs and UEFI boot. Subtracting those two from each enclosure's RAM gives the table's headroom column:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>UGREEN DXP2800:</strong> 8 − 6 − 2 = 0 GB at stock. After the one-slot upgrade to 16 GB, 16 − 8 − 2 = 6 GB, with Immich at its recommended 8 GB.</li>\n<li><strong>TerraMaster F2-425 Plus:</strong> 8 − 6 − 2 = 0 GB at stock. At TerraMaster's 32 GB ceiling, 32 − 8 − 2 = 22 GB. Intel's spec sheet rates the N150 at 16 GB, which gives 16 − 8 − 2 = 6 GB, the same as the DXP2800.</li>\n<li><strong>TerraMaster F2-425:</strong> 4 − 6 = −2 GB before Home Assistant is counted. Immich's no-machine-learning mode needs all 4 GB.</li>\n<li><strong>Synology DS225+:</strong> at its 6 GB maximum, 6 − 8 − 2 = −4 GB. At stock 2 GB it fails Synology's own rule that virtual machines run only on a NAS with more than 2 GB of memory.</li>\n<li><strong>Asustor AS5402T:</strong> 4 − 6 − 2 = −4 GB at stock; 16 − 8 − 2 = 6 GB after filling both slots with 8 GB modules.</li>\n</ul>\n<table>\n<thead><tr><th>Use</th><th>Fits</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>Immich with machine learning plus Home Assistant OS with add-ons, 2 bays</td><td>UGREEN DXP2800 with a 16 GB module</td><td>6 GB left for other containers, Virtual Machine app on the DXP series, lowest maker price of the x86 pair</td></tr>\n<tr><td>The same, with room to grow past 16 GB or to use 5GbE</td><td>TerraMaster F2-425 Plus</td><td>22 GB left at TerraMaster's 32 GB ceiling, three M.2 slots, two 5GbE ports, $9.50 more at the makers' stores</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Cheapest 2-bay file server, Immich without machine learning</td><td>TerraMaster F2-425</td><td>$299.99, but 4 GB leaves no room for Home Assistant OS</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>{buy:ugreen-nasync-dxp2800}</p>\n<h2>Memory budget, VM support and running cost</h2>\n<p>Immich's requirements page also says the Postgres database should live on a local SSD, never a network share, so the M.2 slots matter: the DXP2800 has two, the F2-425 Plus three (ITPro), and the Synology DS225+ none. Synology's Virtual Machine Manager specification states that VMs run only on a NAS with more than 2 GB of memory and only on Btrfs volumes, and that it imports qcow2 images, which is the format Home Assistant publishes for KVM. Synology's DS225+ page lists 2 GB, one slot and a 6 GB maximum, and warns that non-Synology memory modules void complete warranty and technical support. For UGREEN, the esp32.co.uk guide to installing Home Assistant on NASync (3 October 2026) states that current DXP models get Docker and the Virtual Machine app, the DH4300 Plus gets Docker only, and the DH2300 gets neither; it imports the qcow2 image with UEFI boot. Asustor lists VirtualBox as an official ADM app for the AS5402T. We did not verify VM support in TOS 6 on TerraMaster's own pages, so this page makes no claim about it; the F2-425 Plus figures above are hardware only.</p>\n<p>Electricity barely separates the x86 boxes. At the EIA's August 2026 US residential average of 18.16 ¢/kWh, the DXP2800's UGREEN-rated 16.38 W in access is 16.38 × 8.76 = 143.5 kWh, or $26.06 a year. Tim Kutzner at igor'sLAB measured 14.5 W at the wall during transfers with one NVMe SSD and no HDDs, which is 127.0 kWh, or $23.07 a year, and 5.6 W in standby; noise was 33.2 dB(A) at 40 cm, equal to the room floor. Synology's rated 16.98 W for the DS225+ is $27.01 a year. Asustor's rated 22.9 W for the AS5402T is $36.43 a year, about $10 more than the DXP2800.</p>\n<h2>Not recommended</h2>\n<p><strong>Synology DS225+</strong> for this workload. Its 6 GB hard ceiling equals Immich's minimum, sits 2 GB under Immich's recommendation, and leaves nothing for the Home Assistant OS VM; at stock 2 GB Virtual Machine Manager will not run at all, and the only approved upgrade route is Synology's own 4 GB module. <strong>UGREEN DH2300</strong>: no official Docker or VM support in UGOS Pro per the esp32.co.uk guide. <strong>TerraMaster F2-425</strong> at stock: 4 GB means Immich without machine learning and no VM.</p>\n",
 "sources": [("UGREEN DXP2800 price $389.99 at UGREEN's US NAS store, read 2026-11-08", 'https://nas.ugreen.com/products/ugreen-nasync-dxp2800-nas-storage'), ("TerraMaster F2-425 Plus $399.49 at TerraMaster's US store, read 2026-11-08", 'https://www.terra-master.com/products/f2-425-plus'), ("TerraMaster F2-425 $299.99, Intel x86 quad-core, 4 GB RAM, 2.5GbE at TerraMaster's US store, read 2026-11-08", 'https://www.terra-master.com/products/f2-425'), ('Immich requirements: 6 GB minimum, 8 GB recommended, machine learning off at 4 GB, database on local SSD', 'https://docs.immich.app/install/requirements'), ('Home Assistant OS as a VM: 2 GB RAM, 2 vCPUs, UEFI boot, qcow2 image for KVM', 'https://www.home-assistant.io/installation/alternative'), ('Home Assistant Container has no Apps (add-ons), no out-of-the-box Thread or Z-Wave', 'https://www.home-assistant.io/installation/'), ('TerraMaster F2-425 Plus: N150, 8 GB DDR5 in one slot upgradeable to 32 GB, three M.2 NVMe slots, dual 5GbE (ITPro, Dave Mitchell, 23 February 2026)', 'https://www.itpro.com/infrastructure/servers-and-storage/terramaster-f2-425-plus-review-a-versatile-desktop-nas-at-a-great-price'), ('Intel Processor N150 maximum memory 16 GB, one channel', 'https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/products/sku/241636/intel-processor-n150-6m-cache-up-to-3-60-ghz/specifications.html'), ('Intel Processor N100: 4 cores, maximum memory 16 GB, one channel, Quick Sync Video', 'https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/products/sku/231803/intel-processor-n100-6m-cache-up-to-3-40-ghz/specifications.html'), ('UGREEN DXP2800: Intel N100, 8 GB DDR5 expandable to 16 GB, two M.2 slots, one 2.5GbE, 16.38 W access / 5.24 W hibernation (The Gadgeteer, Julian Perry)', 'https://the-gadgeteer.com/2025/10/07/ugreen-nasync-dxp2800-review-another-great-nas/'), ("DXP2800 measured at the wall: 0.6 W off, 5.6 W standby, 14.5 W transferring, 33.2 / 35.6 dB(A) (igor'sLAB, Tim Kutzner)", 'https://www.igorslab.de/ugreen-nasync-dxp2800-nas-im-test/8/'), ('UGOS Pro Docker and Virtual Machine app by model: DXP both, DH4300 Plus Docker only, DH2300 neither; qcow2 import, UEFI (esp32.co.uk, 3 October 2026)', 'https://esp32.co.uk/how-to-install-home-assistant-on-ugreen-nasync/'), ('Synology DS225+: J4125, 2 GB, one slot, 6 GB maximum, no M.2 line in the spec, 16.98 W access, non-Synology memory warranty footnote', 'https://www.synology.com/en-us/products/DS225+#specs'), ('Synology Virtual Machine Manager: VMs only on a NAS with more than 2 GB of memory, Btrfs only, qcow2 import, UEFI boot', 'https://www.synology.com/en-us/dsm/software_spec/vm_manager'), ('Asustor AS5402T: 4 GB in one of two slots, 16 GB maximum, four M.2 PCIe 3.0 x1, VirtualBox app, 22.9 W operation', 'https://www.asustor.com/product/spec?p_id=81'), ('US average residential electricity price 18.16 ¢/kWh, August 2026 (EIA Table 5.6.A)', 'https://www.eia.gov/electricity/monthly/epm_table_grapher.php?t=epmt_5_6_a')],
 "published": '2026-11-03',
 "checked": '2026-11-08',
 "updated": '2026-11-12'},

