{"slug": 'best-solar-generator-kit-under-1000-for-home-backup',
 "question": 'G106 (x18 solar kits: under $1,000 home backup)',
 "method": 'ab-2026-11', "all_links": True, "buy_compare": True,
 "angle": 'B',
 "searched_as": ['best solar generator kits under $1000 2026 EcoFlow Delta 2 Jackery 1000 v2 Bluetti AC180 solar panel price', 'best solar generator kits under $1000 2026 EcoFlow Delta 2 Bluetti AC180 Jackery Explorer 1000 v2 solar panel price', 'best solar generator kits under $1000 2026 EcoFlow Delta 2 Bluetti AC180 Jackery 1000 v2 prices', '2026 best solar generator kits under $1000 200W panel EcoFlow Delta 2 Bluetti AC180 Jackery Explorer 1000 v2 prices', '2026 best solar generator kit under $1000 1000Wh solar panel included EcoFlow Jackery Bluetti prices', 'best solar generator kits under $1000 2026 EcoFlow Delta 2 Jackery 1000 v2 Bluetti AC180 solar panel prices'],
 "title": 'Best solar generator kit under $1,000 for home backup (2026)',
 "h1": 'Best solar generator kit under $1,000 for home backup (2026)',
 "desc": "Six solar generator kits under $1,000 for home backup, compared on battery, panel watts and how much power each kit's own solar panel can keep supplying day and night in November sun. Maker prices checked Nov 14, 2026.",
 "answer": '<p class="lead"><strong>Short answer.</strong> The best solar generator kit under $1,000 for home backup is the ALLPOWERS P1800 (1,024 Wh, 1,800 W) with 600 W solar panel included, $798: in November sun its panel supplies about 66 W around the clock, three times any 200 W kit, and refills the battery in 0.64 day.</p>',
 "columns": [('battery', 'Battery'), ('panel', 'Panel in the kit'), ('solar_max', 'Max solar input'), ('nov_watts', 'November solar, around the clock'), ('refill_days', 'November days to refill'), ('cost_per_watt', 'Price per sustained watt')],
 "rows": [{'slug': 'allpowers-p1800-600w-solar-kit', 'model': 'ALLPOWERS P1800 + 600 W', 'cells': {'battery': '1,024 Wh', 'panel': '600 W', 'solar_max': '650 W', 'nov_watts': '≈66 W', 'refill_days': '0.64 day', 'cost_per_watt': '$12.1'}}, {'slug': 'allpowers-p1800-sp037-solar-kit', 'model': 'ALLPOWERS P1800 + SP037 400 W', 'cells': {'battery': '1,024 Wh', 'panel': '400 W', 'solar_max': '650 W', 'nov_watts': '≈44 W', 'refill_days': '0.97 day', 'cost_per_watt': '$15.8'}}, {'slug': 'allpowers-p1800-sf200-solar-kit', 'model': 'ALLPOWERS P1800 + 200 W', 'cells': {'battery': '1,024 Wh', 'panel': '200 W', 'solar_max': '650 W', 'nov_watts': '≈22 W', 'refill_days': '1.93 days', 'cost_per_watt': '$24.1'}}, {'slug': 'bluetti-ac180-200w-solar-kit', 'model': 'BLUETTI AC180 + 200 W', 'cells': {'battery': '1,152 Wh', 'panel': '200 W', 'solar_max': '500 W', 'nov_watts': '≈22 W', 'refill_days': '2.18 days', 'cost_per_watt': '$34.9'}}, {"asin": 'B0FD3V9LF9', 'brand': 'BLUETTI', 'model': 'Elite 100 V2 + 200 W', 'url': 'https://www.bluettipower.com/products/elite-100-v2-200w-solar', 'cells': {'price': '$729 (maker, 2026-11-14)', 'battery': '1,024 Wh', 'panel': '200 W', 'solar_max': '1,000 W', 'nov_watts': '≈22 W', 'refill_days': '1.93 days', 'cost_per_watt': '$33.0'}}, {'brand': 'EcoFlow', 'model': 'DELTA 3 Classic Solar Generator (160 W)', 'url': 'https://us.ecoflow.com/products/ecoflow-delta-3-classic-solar-generator', 'cells': {'price': '$669 (maker, 2026-11-14)', 'battery': '1,024 Wh', 'panel': '160 W (PowerSized)', 'solar_max': '500 W', 'nov_watts': '≈18 W', 'refill_days': '2.42 days', 'cost_per_watt': '$37.9'}}],
 "after": "\n<h2>What the differences mean</h2><p>In an outage that lasts more than a night, the battery runs out on day one. From then on, the only thing that matters is how much energy the panel puts back each day. Here is the arithmetic behind the table:</p><ul><li><strong>November harvest per rated panel watt:</strong> 3.53 sun-hours (the NREL PVWatts average across 50 US cities) × 0.75 planning derate = 2.65 Wh per day.</li><li><strong>600 W kit:</strong> 600 × 2.65 = 1,589 Wh/day. Spread over 24 h, that is 66 W. The battery refills in 1,024 ÷ 1,589 = 0.64 day.</li><li><strong>Any 200 W kit:</strong> 200 × 2.65 = 530 Wh/day, or 22 W around the clock. The AC180 refills in 1,152 ÷ 530 = 2.2 days.</li><li><strong>Price per sustained watt:</strong> $798 ÷ 66 W = $12 for the 600 W kit, against $769 ÷ 22 W = $35 for the AC180 + 200 W.</li><li><strong>The AC180's bigger battery:</strong> it has 1,152 − 1,024 = 128 Wh more. That equals about 17 minutes of strong sun on the 600 W panel (128 ÷ (600 × 0.75) = 0.28 h).</li><li><strong>Your own load:</strong> take the kWh per year on your fridge's yellow EnergyGuide label and divide by 8.76 to get its average watts. Compare that number with the November solar column.</li></ul><table><thead><tr><th>Your outage</th><th>Kit that fits</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Several days with only solar to recharge</td><td>ALLPOWERS P1800 + 600 W, at 66 W around the clock in November {buy:allpowers-p1800-600w-solar-kit}</td></tr><tr><td>Same idea for $100 less</td><td>ALLPOWERS P1800 + SP037 400 W, at 44 W around the clock {buy:allpowers-p1800-sp037-solar-kit}</td></tr><tr><td>One night on the battery alone</td><td>BLUETTI AC180 + 200 W, the largest battery here at 1,152 Wh {buy:bluetti-ac180-200w-solar-kit}</td></tr><tr><td>Desktop PC or NAS that must not reboot</td><td>EcoFlow DELTA 3 Classic. EcoFlow rates its switchover under 10 ms, and BLUETTI rates the AC180 at 20 ms.</td></tr><tr><td>Adding panels later</td><td>BLUETTI Elite 100 V2 + 200 W, which takes up to 1,000 W of solar</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>How much the panel puts back in a November outage</h2><p>A panel's rated watts assume full sun at noon. A November day in the US averages 3.53 peak sun-hours (December 2.87), and folding panels deliver about 75% of their rating once angle, heat and wiring losses are counted. Averaged over the whole day, each kit's panel can only keep that much flowing. Every 200 W kit lands near 22 W, so the gap between a 1,024 Wh and a 1,152 Wh battery matters less than the gap between a 200 W and a 600 W panel. A panel only counts in full if the station accepts it. ALLPOWERS rates the P1800 for 650 W of solar, so its 600 W panel is not clipped. BLUETTI's AC180 accepts up to 500 W (12–60 V, 10 A), which means a 200 W panel uses less than half of its input.</p><p>Battery ratings also overstate what reaches the outlets. OutdoorGearLab drained the AC180 at 80% load and measured 950 Wh of its rated 1,152 Wh. Similar inverter losses apply to every kit in the table, so compare the kits by the panel figures above.</p><p>One pricing trap: BLUETTI sells the same AC180 + 200 W bundle at $769 on its /products/ac180 listing and at $999 on its solar-generator-ac180 listing (both read 2026-11-14). Check which page you are on before you pay.</p><h2>Not recommended</h2><p><strong>Anker SOLIX S2000 as a kit under $1,000.</strong> Anker's own US store sells the 2,010 Wh S2000 alone for $699.99. Its cheapest panel bundle, the S2000 + 400 W, costs $1,199.99, which is over budget. If you pair the S2000 with a single 200 W panel instead, refilling it would take 2,010 ÷ 530 = 3.8 November days, and its 1,500 W rated output is the lowest of the stations here.</p>\n",
 "sources": [('ALLPOWERS P1800 + 600 W kit price $798, compare-at $1,059.98 (read 2026-11-14)', 'https://iallpowers.com/products/allpowers-1800w-solar-generator-p1800-1024wh-with-600w-solar-panel'), ('ALLPOWERS P1800 + 400 W kit price $698 (read 2026-11-14)', 'https://iallpowers.com/products/allpowers-1800w-solar-generator-p1800-1024wh-with-400w-solar-panel'), ('ALLPOWERS P1800 + 200 W kit price $531 (read 2026-11-14)', 'https://iallpowers.com/products/allpowers-1800w-solar-generator-p1800-1024wh-with-200w-solar-panel'), ('P1800 1,024 Wh, 1,800 W (3,600 W peak), up to 650 W solar via XT60, over 3,000 cycles (read 2026-11-14)', 'https://iallpowers.com/products/allpowers-p1800-portable-power-station-1024wh-1800w'), ('ALLPOWERS SP039 600 W folding panel: 44 V, 27.5 lb folded, MC4-to-XT60 cable included (read 2026-11-14)', 'https://iallpowers.com/products/allpowers-sp039-600w-monocrystalline-portable-solar-panel'), ('ALLPOWERS warranty policy: 24 months from date of purchase by default; 5-year tier lists R-series and S2000/S700 models, not the P1800; SP039 panel 2-year limited warranty (read 2026-11-14)', 'https://iallpowers.com/pages/warranty-policy'), ('ALLPOWERS refund policy: 30 days after receiving the item to request a return; item unused, in original packaging, with proof of purchase (read 2026-11-14)', 'https://iallpowers.com/policies/refund-policy'), ('US average solar resource: November 3.53, December 2.87 kWh/m²/day, NREL PVWatts averaged over 50 cities (read 2026-11-14)', 'https://shrinkthatfootprint.com/?p=4385'), ('75% planning derate for portable panels; DELTA 3 Classic $669 kit listed with 160 W panel (read 2026-11-14)', 'https://powersized.com/solar-generator-kits/'), ('BLUETTI AC180 + 200 W Solar $769, compare-at $899 (read 2026-11-14)', 'https://www.bluettipower.com/products/ac180?variant=45427542491355'), ('AC180 500 W max solar, 12–60 V, 10 A; 20 ms switchover (read 2026-11-14)', 'https://www.bluettipower.com/pages/ac180'), ('Same AC180 + 200 W bundle listed at $999 on a second BLUETTI listing (read 2026-11-14)', 'https://www.bluettipower.com/products/solar-generator-ac180'), ('BLUETTI Elite 100 V2 + 200 W $729, 1,024 Wh, 1,000 W solar input (read 2026-11-14)', 'https://www.bluettipower.com/products/elite-100-v2-200w-solar'), ('EcoFlow DELTA 3 Classic Solar Generator $669 (read 2026-11-14)', 'https://us.ecoflow.com/products/ecoflow-delta-3-classic-solar-generator'), ('DELTA 3 Classic under 10 ms switchover, 500 W max PV input (read 2026-11-14)', 'https://www.ecoflow.com/us/delta-3-classic-portable-power-station'), ('OutdoorGearLab measured 950 Wh usable from the 1,152 Wh AC180 (read 2026-11-14)', 'https://www.outdoorgearlab.com/reviews/camping-and-hiking/power-station/bluetti-ac180'), ('Anker SOLIX S2000 $699.99 alone, S2000 + 400 W $1,199.99, 2,010 Wh, 1,500 W (read 2026-11-14)', 'https://www.ankersolix.com/products/s2000-portable-power-station')],
 "published": '2026-11-04',
 "checked": '2026-11-14',
 "updated": '2026-11-14'},

