{"slug": '1000wh-power-station-with-400w-solar-panel-bundle',
 "question": 'G107 (x18 solar kits: 1 kWh station bundled with 400 W)',
 "method": 'ab-2026-11', "all_links": True, "buy_compare": True,
 "angle": 'E',
 "searched_as": ['1000Wh power station 400W solar panel bundle EcoFlow Jackery Bluetti price 2026', '1000Wh power station 400W solar panel bundle EcoFlow Jackery Bluetti 2026', '1000Wh power station 400W solar panel bundle EcoFlow Bluetti Jackery 2026'],
 "title": '1,000 Wh power station bundled with a 400 W solar panel (2026): every kit we found',
 "h1": '1,000 Wh power stations sold with a 400 W solar panel (2026)',
 "desc": "1,000 Wh power stations sold bundled with a 400 W solar panel, priced at BLUETTI's and ALLPOWERS's US stores on 2026-11-08 and ranked on lab-measured energy from Outdoor Life, StorageReview, Notebookcheck and OutdoorGearLab.",
 "answer": '<p class="lead"><strong>Short answer.</strong> For a 1000 Wh power station bundled with a 400 W solar panel, get the BLUETTI AC180 + 2 × 200 W bundle: its 1,152 Wh battery delivered 980–1,030 Wh in Outdoor Life and StorageReview tests, more than the EcoFlow, Jackery or Anker 1 kWh units measured (850–910 Wh).</p>',
 "columns": [('capacity', 'Battery (rated)'), ('measured', 'AC energy delivered in a lab test'), ('solar', 'Solar input limit'), ('panel', 'Panels in the box')],
 "rows": [{'slug': 'bluetti-ac180-2x200w-solar-kit', 'model': 'BLUETTI AC180 + 2 × 200 W solar kit', 'cells': {'capacity': '1,152 Wh', 'measured': '980 Wh at ~380 W, 85% (Outdoor Life); 1,030 Wh at 350 W, 89% (StorageReview)', 'solar': '500 W, 12–60 V, 10 A: 400 W needs 40 V+, so wire the panels in series', 'panel': '2 × 200 W SP200L'}}, {'slug': 'allpowers-p1800-sp037-solar-kit', 'model': 'ALLPOWERS P1800 + SP037 400 W', 'cells': {'capacity': '1,024 Wh', 'measured': "No published lab run-down of the P1800; ALLPOWERS's S2000 Pro gave 61% of its rating (StorageReview)", 'solar': '650 W max (XT60)', 'panel': '1 × 400 W SP037 (37.4 V listed)'}}, {'slug': 'allpowers-s2000-pro-sp037-solar-kit', 'model': 'ALLPOWERS S2000 Pro + SP037 400 W', 'cells': {'capacity': '1,451.5 Wh', 'measured': '920 Wh at 350 W, 61% of a 1,500 Wh-rated 2023 unit (StorageReview)', 'solar': '650 W, 18–70 V, 18 A (StorageReview, 2023 unit)', 'panel': '1 × 400 W SP037'}}, {'slug': 'bluetti-ac180-200w-solar-kit', 'model': 'BLUETTI AC180 + 200 W kit, plus a second SP200L', 'cells': {'capacity': '1,152 Wh', 'measured': 'Same station: 980–1,030 Wh (Outdoor Life, StorageReview)', 'solar': 'Same 10 A cap: series wiring for the full 400 W', 'panel': '1 × 200 W in the kit; add a $399 SP200L for 400 W ($1,168 total)'}}],
 "after": "\n<h2>What the differences mean</h2><ul><li><strong>Share of the rating you actually get:</strong> AC180 980 ÷ 1,152 = 85% (Outdoor Life) and 1,030 ÷ 1,152 = 89% (StorageReview). S2000 Pro 920 ÷ 1,500 = 61% (StorageReview, 2023 unit).</li><li><strong>Cost per delivered Wh:</strong> AC180 bundle $1,232 ÷ 980 Wh = $1.26. AC180 + 200 W kit plus a second SP200L, $1,168 ÷ 980 Wh = $1.19. S2000 Pro + SP037, $848 ÷ 920 Wh = $0.92.</li><li><strong>Bundle against parts:</strong> at BLUETTI, $499 AC180 + 2 × $399 SP200L = $1,297 bought separately, so the $1,232 bundle saves $65. The $769 AC180 + 200 W kit + one $399 SP200L = $1,168, which is $64 under the bundle. At ALLPOWERS, the $399 P1800 + the $299 SP037 flash deal = $698, the kit price to the dollar, so that bundle saves nothing over the parts.</li><li><strong>Fastest solar refill at full panel rating:</strong> AC180 1,152 Wh ÷ 400 W = 2.9 h. P1800 1,024 Wh ÷ 400 W = 2.6 h. Both are before charging losses.</li><li><strong>Panel voltage the AC180 needs:</strong> 400 W ÷ 10 A = 40 V across the array.</li></ul><table><thead><tr><th>Use</th><th>Kit</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Longest runtime per charge, shipping now</td><td>BLUETTI AC180 + 2 × 200 W</td><td>Most lab-measured energy: 980–1,030 Wh</td></tr><tr><td>Lowest outlay for 1 kWh + 400 W</td><td>ALLPOWERS P1800 + SP037 {buy:allpowers-p1800-sp037-solar-kit}</td><td>$698; ALLPOWERS's store data doesn't separate pre-order from in-stock, so check the ship date at checkout</td></tr><tr><td>Most delivered energy per dollar</td><td>ALLPOWERS S2000 Pro + SP037 {buy:allpowers-s2000-pro-sp037-solar-kit}</td><td>$0.92 per delivered Wh, but a 1.45 kWh station weighing 31.97 lb (StorageReview)</td></tr><tr><td>Overnight CPAP or laptop</td><td>Any of them</td><td>At ~34 W, Outdoor Life got 620 Wh from the AC180 and 530 Wh from the EcoFlow DELTA 3</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>How much energy a 1 kWh station really gives</h2><p>A station's rated Wh is the capacity of its cells. What reaches your appliance is lower, because the inverter, the battery management system and a reserve at the bottom of the pack all take a share. The figures below were measured by named labs running each station from full to empty:</p><table><thead><tr><th>Station</th><th>Rated</th><th>Delivered</th><th>Load / lab</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>BLUETTI AC180</td><td>1,152 Wh</td><td>1,030 Wh</td><td>350 W, StorageReview; 1,360 Wh from the wall to refill, so 1,030 ÷ 1,360 = 76% round trip</td></tr><tr><td>BLUETTI AC180</td><td>1,152 Wh</td><td>980 Wh (950 Wh after 3 months in a garage)</td><td>~380 W dehumidifier, Outdoor Life</td></tr><tr><td>ALLPOWERS S2000 Pro</td><td>1,500 Wh (2023 unit)</td><td>920 Wh</td><td>350 W, StorageReview</td></tr><tr><td>EcoFlow DELTA 3 Plus</td><td>1,024 Wh</td><td>910 Wh; 1,180 Wh in to recharge</td><td>StorageReview (load not stated)</td></tr><tr><td>Jackery Explorer 1000 v2</td><td>1,070 Wh</td><td>910 Wh</td><td>OutdoorGearLab (load not stated)</td></tr><tr><td>EcoFlow DELTA 3</td><td>1,024 Wh</td><td>900 Wh</td><td>~380 W, Outdoor Life</td></tr><tr><td>Anker SOLIX C1000 Gen 2</td><td>1,024 Wh</td><td>850 Wh</td><td>~250 W, Notebookcheck (EU 230 V unit)</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Small loads come out worse. On a ~34 W grow light, Outdoor Life got 620 Wh from the AC180 over 15.1 h and 530 Wh from the DELTA 3 over 13.9 h, about half the rating. The inverter's own draw counts for more when the load is small.</p><p><strong>Wiring the AC180 kit.</strong> BLUETTI rates the AC180's solar input at 500 W max, 12–60 V Voc and 10 A. Two 200 W panels in parallel run at a single panel's voltage, which is well under the 40 V needed, so the 10 A cap holds them below 400 W. Wired in series, the voltages add and the pair can deliver its full rating. Keep the series total under 60 V Voc, and use two panels of the same model. If you take the cheaper route ({buy:bluetti-ac180-200w-solar-kit}), BLUETTI's variant listing doesn't name the kit's 200 W panel, so check that it is an SP200L before adding a second one.</p><p><strong>The Anker kit.</strong> Anker's US page lists the C1000 Gen 2 + 400 W bifacial bundle as shipping from early December, but showed no price on 2026-11-08, so it isn't in the priced table. The C1000 Gen 2 takes 14.5 A only from 29–60 V. Below 29 V it takes 8.2 A, which caps a panel at 28 V × 8.2 A = 230 W. A 400 W panel therefore has to run at 29 V or more to deliver its full output.</p>\n",
 "sources": [('BLUETTI AC180 + 2×200W kit $1,232 orderable; AC180 $499; AC180 + 200W kit $769 (read 2026-11-08)', 'https://www.bluettipower.com/products/ac180'), ('AC180 specs: 1,152 Wh, 500 W / 12–60 V / 10 A solar input, 35.27 lb, 3,500+ cycles to 80%, 5-year warranty (read 2026-11-08)', 'https://www.bluettipower.com/pages/ac180'), ('BLUETTI refund policy: 30-day return for complete, unused items in original packaging; return shipping deducted from refund (read 2026-11-08)', 'https://www.bluettipower.com/policies/refund-policy'), ('BLUETTI SP200L 200 W panel $399 (read 2026-11-08)', 'https://www.bluettipower.com/products/bluetti-sp200l-solar-panel-200w'), ('Outdoor Life lab tests: AC180 980 Wh at ~380 W, 950 Wh after storage, 620 Wh at ~34 W; EcoFlow DELTA 3 900 Wh and 530 Wh (read 2026-11-08)', 'https://www.outdoorlife.com/gear/best-portable-power-stations-2026/'), ('StorageReview: AC180 1,030 Wh at 350 W, 1,360 Wh to recharge (read 2026-11-08)', 'https://www.storagereview.com/review/bluetti-ac180-portable-power-station-review'), ('StorageReview: EcoFlow DELTA 3 Plus 910 Wh out, 1,180 Wh in (read 2026-11-08)', 'https://www.storagereview.com/review/ecoflow-delta-3-plus-review'), ('Notebookcheck: Anker SOLIX C1000 Gen 2 850 Wh at ~250 W, EU unit (read 2026-11-08)', 'https://www.notebookcheck.net/Lighter-stronger-and-faster-but-Anker-Solix-C1000-Gen-2-power-station-review.1190194.0.html'), ('OutdoorGearLab: Jackery Explorer 1000 v2 910 Wh of 1,070 Wh (read 2026-11-08)', 'https://www.outdoorgearlab.com/reviews/camping-and-hiking/power-station/jackery-explorer-1000-v2'), ('StorageReview: ALLPOWERS S2000 Pro 920 Wh at 350 W of a claimed 1,500 Wh; 650 W, 18–70 V, 18 A solar; 31.97 lb (read 2026-11-08)', 'https://www.storagereview.com/review/allpowers-s2000-pro-portable-power-station-review'), ('ALLPOWERS P1800 + 400 W kit $698 at the ALLPOWERS US store (read 2026-11-08)', 'https://iallpowers.com/products/allpowers-1800w-solar-generator-p1800-1024wh-with-400w-solar-panel'), ('ALLPOWERS P1800 alone $399; 1,024 Wh; 650 W solar via XT60 (read 2026-11-08)', 'https://iallpowers.com/products/allpowers-p1800-portable-power-station-1024wh-1800w'), ('ALLPOWERS SP037 400 W flash deal $299; 37.4 V output listed (read 2026-11-08)', 'https://iallpowers.com/products/allpowers-sp037-polycrystalline-portable-solar-panel-400w-flash-deal'), ('ALLPOWERS S2000 Pro + SP037 kit $848 (read 2026-11-08)', 'https://iallpowers.com/products/allpowers-solar-generator-kit-2400w-s2000-pro-sp037-400w-solar-panel'), ('ALLPOWERS S2000 Pro + 200 W kit listing: S2000 Pro 1,451.5 Wh (read 2026-11-08)', 'https://iallpowers.com/products/s2000-pro-200w-solar-panel'), ('Anker SOLIX C1000 Gen 2: 1,024 Wh, MPPT 11–28 V 8.2 A / 29–60 V 14.5 A, 400 W bundle ships early December, no price shown (read 2026-11-08)', 'https://www.ankersolix.com/products/c1000-gen2')],
 "published": '2026-11-04',
 "checked": '2026-11-08',
 "updated": '2026-11-12'},

