# ---------------- G152: best-quiet-gaming-controller (gap mining daily) ----------------
# ---------------- best-quiet-gaming-controller (research method ab-2026-11, 2026-11-08) ----------------
{"slug": 'best-quiet-gaming-controller',
 "question": 'G152 (brand page for EasySMX: quiet gaming controller)',
 "method": 'ab-2026-11', "all_links": True,
 "angle": 'A',
 "searched_as": ['quietest gaming controllers membrane buttons quiet dpad triggers reviews 2026', 'quietest gaming controller silent buttons membrane controller reviews 8bitdo gamesir', 'quietest gaming controllers silent buttons membrane triggers reviews GameSir 8BitDo 2026'],
 "title": 'Best Quiet Gaming Controller (2026): Picks for Late-Night and Shared-Room Play',
 "h1": 'Best quiet gaming controller',
 "desc": 'Which buttons each quiet controller actually silences: Mobapad Chitu 2 Silent, EasySMX X05 Pro, GameSir Super Nova and EasySMX S05 Pro compared by face buttons, D-pad, triggers and battery.',
 "answer": '<p class="lead"><strong>Short answer.</strong> For a quiet gaming controller, the quietest is the Mobapad Chitu 2 HD Silent Edition: silicone, not microswitch, under the face buttons, D-pad, bumpers and triggers, plus silent silicone stick rings. The cheaper EasySMX X05 Pro keeps metal dome switches under its D-pad.</p>',
 "columns": [('quiet', 'What is silenced'), ('dpad', 'D-pad'), ('platforms', 'Platforms'), ('runtime', 'Battery per charge')],
 "rows": [{"asin": 'B0GY8P8278', 'brand': 'Mobapad', 'model': 'Chitu 2 HD Silent Edition', 'url': 'https://www.mobapad.com/products/mobapad-chitu-2-hd-switch-2-controller-silent-edition', 'cells': {'quiet': 'Liquid silicone under ABXY, D-pad, bumpers, triggers and +/−, plus silicone stick tracks (HLPLANET)', 'dpad': 'Liquid silicone, fixed classic-cross cap (HLPLANET)', 'platforms': 'PC, Switch, Switch 2, Android, iOS (HLPLANET)', 'runtime': 'About 15 h with regular use, standard Chitu 2 on the same 1,000 mAh battery (HLPLANET)', 'price': '$49.99 (maker, 2026-11-08)'}}, {'slug': 'easysmx-x05-pro', 'model': 'EasySMX X05 Pro', 'cells': {'quiet': "'Noise-dampening silicone' for the buttons, none named (EasySMX); stick clicks still audible (GamingOnLinux)", 'dpad': "'Metal dome switches' (EasySMX); 'a clear click you can feel' (GamingOnLinux)", 'platforms': 'PC, Switch, mobile, handhelds; 2.4 GHz, Bluetooth, wired (EasySMX)', 'runtime': 'About 6 h (HLPLANET test)'}}, {"asin": 'B0DPMGDZLZ', 'brand': 'GameSir', 'model': 'Super Nova', 'url': 'https://shop.gamesir.com/products/gamesir-super-nova', 'cells': {'quiet': "Names ABXY only: 'silent ABXY buttons' (GameSir)", 'dpad': 'Membrane (GameSir spec sheet)', 'platforms': 'PC, Switch, Android, iOS (GameSir)', 'runtime': '18 h recorded (Wccftech)', 'price': '$49.99 (maker, 2026-11-08)'}}, {'slug': 'easysmx-s05-pro', 'model': 'EasySMX S05 Pro', 'cells': {'quiet': "'Silicone-damped buttons', none named (EasySMX)", 'dpad': "'Smooth disc-pivot D-pad' (EasySMX's wording)", 'platforms': 'Switch, Switch 2, one-button wake-up (EasySMX)', 'runtime': 'Up to 20 h, dock in box (EasySMX claim)'}}],
 "after": "\n<h2>What the differences mean</h2><ul><li><strong>Silenced button groups:</strong> Chitu 2 Silent 5 of 5 (ABXY, D-pad, bumpers, triggers, +/−), Super Nova 1 of 5 (ABXY). EasySMX names none for the X05 Pro or S05 Pro, so the ear tests below are what tell you.</li><li><strong>Price gap:</strong> X05 Pro against Super Nova: $49.99 − $35.99 = $14.00 saved. S05 Pro against X05 Pro: $54.99 − $35.99 = $19.00 more, with a charging dock in the box.</li><li><strong>Nights per charge at 2 hours a night:</strong> X05 Pro 6 ÷ 2 = 3; Chitu 2 15 ÷ 2 = 7.5; Super Nova 18 ÷ 2 = 9; S05 Pro 20 ÷ 2 = 10 (maker claim, not a test).</li></ul><table><thead><tr><th>Use</th><th>Fits best</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Playing beside someone asleep, Switch 2 or PC</td><td>Mobapad Chitu 2 HD Silent Edition</td></tr><tr><td>D-pad-heavy games (platformers, fighters), played quietly</td><td>Chitu 2 Silent (silicone D-pad) or GameSir Super Nova (membrane D-pad)</td></tr><tr><td>PC or Steam Deck on the smallest budget</td><td>EasySMX X05 Pro</td></tr><tr><td>Switch with a charging dock included</td><td>EasySMX S05 Pro</td></tr><tr><td>Xbox</td><td>GameSir G7 SE (wired; HLPLANET lists membrane face buttons, though GameSir makes no quiet claim)</td></tr><tr><td>PS5</td><td>Sony DualSense with vibration and trigger effects turned off (see below)</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>What “quiet” actually covers on each controller</h2><p>Most of the noise comes from the switch under each button. EasySMX's own explainer says microswitch buttons “often produce a clear click when activated”. Rubber membranes “usually sound softer” but can still make noise when the keycap bottoms out or returns. It also warns that “strong rumble can create greater room noise than the buttons”. None of these four makers publishes a decibel figure, so the comparison rests on what each maker says it silenced and on named reviewers' ear tests.</p><p><strong>Mobapad Chitu 2 HD Silent Edition.</strong> In HLPLANET's spec table (Snimtas, 2026-05-21), every button that uses a microswitch on the standard model uses liquid silicone rubber on the Silent Edition. That covers ABXY, D-pad, triggers, bumpers and +/−. The sticks also glide on silicone tracks instead of hitting a hard plastic ring, with “almost no sound at all when you move the sticks”. No other pad here deals with stick-ring knock. HLPLANET calls it “one of the quietest controllers you can get (and maybe even the quietest overall)”. The trade-off: the D-pad cap is fixed.</p><p><strong>EasySMX X05 Pro.</strong> EasySMX says its buttons use “restructured mechanics and noise-dampening silicone” but does not list which ones. Its launch post describes an “8-Directional D-Pad with metal dome switches”. Two named ear tests split. Eric Hauter (Gaming Nexus, 2025-11-14) found the face buttons “not loud, but nothing special” with a small “pop”. He found the triggers, bumpers and D-pad “extraordinarily quiet”, and called it “definitely the quietest” of his many controllers. Liam Squires-Hand (GamingOnLinux, 2025-11-10) found “every other button is pretty much a whisper” apart from the thumbstick clicks, and felt “a clear click” on the D-pad. He also hit a trigger fault where light presses read as full pulls, which he called “a complete deal-breaker”. It is still the cheapest controller here with a maker quiet claim. {buy:easysmx-x05-pro}</p><p><strong>GameSir Super Nova.</strong> GameSir limits its claim to “silent ABXY buttons”. Its spec sheet lists a membrane D-pad, but it makes no quiet claim for the bumpers or triggers.</p><p><strong>EasySMX S05 Pro.</strong> EasySMX promises “silicone-damped buttons” and a “smooth disc-pivot D-pad”, with Switch 2 wake-up and a dock. We have no named ear test for it yet. {buy:easysmx-s05-pro}</p><p><strong>Turn the rumble down too.</strong> Quiet buttons don't help if the motors buzz against a desk. On PS5, Sony's controller settings have <em>Vibration Intensity</em> and <em>Trigger Effect Intensity</em> under Settings &gt; Accessories &gt; Controller (General). Lower both to quiet the DualSense's motors and trigger effects.</p><h2>Not recommended</h2><p><strong>EasySMX X05 (non-Pro) for quiet play.</strong> It looks like the X05 Pro and costs $29.99, $6.00 less, but EasySMX's listing makes no quiet-button claim for it. If silence is the reason you're buying, get the Pro.</p>\n",
 "sources": [('Chitu 2 HD Silent Edition price $49.99 (Mobapad store, read 2026-11-08)', 'https://www.mobapad.com/products/mobapad-chitu-2-hd-switch-2-controller-silent-edition'), ("Chitu 2 HD Silent Edition: liquid silicone on ABXY, D-pad, triggers, bumpers, +/−; silicone stick tracks; platforms PC, Switch 1/2, Android, iOS; fixed classic-cross D-pad cap; 1,000 mAh; 'maybe even the quietest overall' (Snimtas, read 2026-11-08)", 'https://www.hlplanet.com/mobapad-chitu-2-hd-standard-vs-silent/'), ("Standard Chitu 2 runtime 'about 15 hours or so with regular use' on 1,000 mAh (Fang, HLPLANET review, read 2026-11-08)", 'https://www.hlplanet.com/?p=8180'), ('X05 Pro price $35.99, platforms and connections (EasySMX, read 2026-11-08)', 'https://www.easysmx.com/products/easysmx-x05pro-multiplatform-wireless-gaming-controller-with-noise-canceling-button'), ("X05 Pro 'restructured mechanics and noise-dampening silicone', '8-Directional D-Pad with metal dome switches', $35.99 MSRP (EasySMX launch post, read 2026-11-08)", 'https://www.easysmx.com/blogs/easysmx-news/easysmx-release-x05pro-quiet-controller-for-entry-to-mid-level-players'), ("X05 Pro ear test: face buttons 'nothing special', triggers, bumpers and D-pad 'extraordinarily quiet', 'definitely the quietest' (Eric Hauter, read 2026-11-08)", 'https://www.gamingnexus.com/Article/16307/EasySMX-X05-Pro/'), ("X05 Pro ear test: 'pretty much a whisper' except stick clicks, D-pad 'a clear click', trigger fault (Liam Squires-Hand, read 2026-11-08)", 'https://gamingonlinux.com/2025/11/the-easysmx-x05-pro-wireless-controller-is-cheap-feature-filled-and-comfortable-with-a-big-flaw'), ('X05 Pro runtime about 6 h, tested (Franciszek Ziemian, HLPLANET review, read 2026-11-08)', 'https://www.hlplanet.com/?p=6813'), ("Super Nova price $49.99, 'silent ABXY buttons', platforms (GameSir store, read 2026-11-08)", 'https://shop.gamesir.com/products/gamesir-super-nova'), ("Super Nova spec sheet: ABXY membrane, D-pad membrane; platforms; $49.99; 'silent ABXY buttons' (GameSir, read 2026-11-08)", 'https://gamesir.com/products/gamesir-super-nova/buy'), ('Super Nova 18-hour session recorded (Muhammad Zuhair, read 2026-11-08)', 'https://wccftech.com/review/gamesir-supernova-controller-review-aesthetics-optimal-wireless-experience-in-one-package/'), ('S05 Pro price $54.99, silicone-damped buttons, disc-pivot D-pad, Switch 2 wake-up, up to 20 h, dock (EasySMX, read 2026-11-08)', 'https://www.easysmx.com/products/easysmx-s05-pro-switch-gaming-controller-for-switch-2-wake-up-tmr-sticks-whisphertech-button-immersive-rumble'), ('Why controllers are loud; microswitch vs membrane; rumble can be louder than buttons (EasySMX, read 2026-11-08)', 'https://www.easysmx.com/blogs/easysmx-controllers/why-gaming-controllers-are-loud'), ('PS5 Vibration Intensity and Trigger Effect Intensity under Settings > Accessories > Controller (General) (PlayStation Support, read 2026-11-08)', 'https://www.playstation.com/en-us/support/hardware/adjust-general-controller-settings/'), ('GameSir G7 SE membrane face buttons, wired, Xbox and PC (HLPLANET, read 2026-11-08)', 'https://www.hlplanet.com/gamesir-g7-vs-g7se/'), ('GameSir G7 SE product page: Xbox and PC, wired, no quiet-button claim (GameSir, read 2026-11-08)', 'https://gamesir.com/products/gamesir-g7-se'), ('EasySMX X05 price $29.99, no quiet-button claim (EasySMX, read 2026-11-08)', 'https://www.easysmx.com/products/easysmx%C2%AE-x05-multiplatform-gaming-controller-with-hall-effect-joysticks')],
 "published": '2026-11-06',
 "checked": '2026-11-08',
 "updated": '2026-11-12'},

