{"slug": 'best-lifepo4-battery-charger',
 "question": 'G158 (gap mining daily: lifepo4 charger, 2890 Bing searches / 3 mo, coverage 0.194)',
 "method": 'ab-2026-11', "all_links": True,
 "angle": 'B',
 "searched_as": ['Victron Blue Smart IP65 Li-ion mode 12V 15A NOCO GENIUS10 lithium LiTime 14.6V 20A specifications', 'Victron Blue Smart IP65 lithium mode 12 15 NOCO GENIUS10 lithium LiTime 14.6V 20A specifications', 'best LiFePO4 charger NOCO GENIUS10 Victron Blue Smart IP65 LiTime 2026 specifications lithium'],
 "title": 'Best LiFePO4 Battery Charger (12 V) in 2026: Redodo 20A vs LiTime, NOCO, Victron',
 "h1": 'Best LiFePO4 battery charger for 12 V batteries',
 "desc": 'Cost per amp decides it. The Redodo 14.6V 20A costs $4.15 per amp, against $5.15 for the LiTime 20A, $9.99 for the NOCO GENIUS10 and $11.73 for the Victron Blue Smart IP65 12/15. Also compared: lithium charge voltages and 100 Ah refill times.',
 "answer": '<p class="lead"><strong>Short answer.</strong> The best LiFePO4 battery charger for a 12V lithium battery is the Redodo 14.6V 20A: it charges to 14.6V and refills 100 Ah in about 5 h at $4.15 per amp, against $5.15 for the LiTime 20A, $9.99 for the NOCO GENIUS10 and $11.73 for the Victron Blue Smart IP65 12V 15A.</p>',
 "columns": [('current', 'Charge current'), ('per_amp', 'Cost per amp'), ('refill', '100 Ah refill, constant-current stage'), ('volts', 'LiFePO4 charge voltage')],
 "rows": [{'slug': 'redodo-14-6v-20a-lifepo4-charger', 'model': 'Redodo 14.6V 20A LiFePO4 Charger', 'cells': {'current': '20 A', 'per_amp': '$4.15 ($82.99 ÷ 20 A)', 'refill': '5.0 h (maker: 50% in 2.5 h)', 'volts': '14.6 V, then shuts off'}}, {"asin": 'B08PZ7LBT6', 'brand': 'LiTime', 'model': '12V (14.6V) 20A LiFePO4 Charger', 'url': 'https://www.litime.com/products/12v-20a-lifepo4-battery-charger', 'cells': {'price': '$102.99 (maker, 2026-11-08)', 'current': '20 A', 'per_amp': '$5.15 ($102.99 ÷ 20 A)', 'refill': '5.0 h', 'volts': '14.6 V'}}, {'slug': 'redodo-14-6v-10a-lifepo4-charger', 'model': 'Redodo 14.6V 10A LiFePO4 Charger', 'cells': {'current': '10 A', 'per_amp': '$6.00 ($59.99 ÷ 10 A)', 'refill': '10 h (maker: 50 Ah to 50% in 2.5 h)', 'volts': '14.6 V, then shuts off'}}, {"asin": 'B0FMK3CPQH', 'brand': 'LiTime', 'model': '12V (14.6V) 40A Mountable Charger', 'url': 'https://www.litime.com/products/40a-charger-for-12v-lifepo4-battery', 'cells': {'price': '$167.19 (maker, 2026-11-08)', 'current': '40 A', 'per_amp': '$4.18 ($167.19 ÷ 40 A)', 'refill': '2.5 h (maker: 200 Ah in 5 h)', 'volts': '14.6 V'}}, {'slug': 'redodo-14-6v-40a-lifepo4-charger', 'model': 'Redodo 14.6V 40A Ultra Fast LiFePO4 Charger', 'cells': {'current': '40 A', 'per_amp': '$4.50 ($179.99 ÷ 40 A)', 'refill': '2.5 h (maker: 200 Ah in about 5 h)', 'volts': '14.6 V; pre-charge from 0 V'}}, {'brand': 'Victron Energy', 'model': 'Blue Smart IP65 12/15 (120 V)', 'url': 'https://www.victronenergy.com/chargers/blue-smart-ip65-charger', 'cells': {'price': '$175.95 (Solar-Electric, 2026-11-08)', 'current': '15 A (4 A low mode)', 'per_amp': '$11.73 ($175.95 ÷ 15 A)', 'refill': '6.7 h', 'volts': '14.2 V, then 13.5 V storage (Li-ion mode)'}}, {'brand': 'NOCO', 'model': 'GENIUS10', 'url': 'https://no.co/genius10', 'cells': {'price': '$99.87 (Clamp & Crank listing, 2026-11-08)', 'current': '10 A', 'per_amp': '$9.99 ($99.87 ÷ 10 A)', 'refill': '10 h', 'volts': 'About 14.2 V top-off, about 13.6 V hold (Auto Median, measured)'}}],
 "after": "\n<h2>What the differences mean</h2><p>Cost per amp is the price divided by the rated charge current. Refill time is the battery's amp-hours divided by that current, which covers the constant-current stage only. The final top-off adds a little: Victron's own worked example is 9.5 h of bulk charging plus about 0.5 h of absorption for 100 Ah on a 10 A charger.</p><ul><li>Redodo 20A: $82.99 ÷ 20 A = $4.15 per amp. 100 Ah ÷ 20 A = 5.0 h. 200 Ah ÷ 20 A = 10 h.</li><li>LiTime 20A: $102.99 ÷ 20 A = $5.15 per amp. That is $20.00 more than the Redodo for the same 20 A at 14.6 V.</li><li>Victron 12/15: $175.95 ÷ 15 A = $11.73 per amp, 2.8× the Redodo's. 100 Ah ÷ 15 A = 6.7 h. It costs $92.96 more and delivers 5 A less.</li><li>NOCO GENIUS10: $99.87 ÷ 10 A = $9.99 per amp, 2.4× the Redodo's. 100 Ah ÷ 10 A = 10 h.</li><li>Peak power: 20 A × 14.6 V = 292 W for the 20 A chargers. The Victron in Li-ion mode gives 15 A × 14.2 V = 213 W, so the 20 A chargers deliver 37% more.</li><li>At 40 A the order flips: LiTime $167.19 ÷ 40 A = $4.18 per amp against Redodo $179.99 ÷ 40 A = $4.50, a gap of $12.80.</li></ul><table><thead><tr><th>Your battery and use</th><th>Fits</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>One 12 V 100 Ah LiFePO4, recharged between trips</td><td>Redodo 14.6V 20A</td><td>Lowest cost per amp of any 10–20 A charger here, and about 5 h to full. {buy:redodo-14-6v-20a-lifepo4-charger}</td></tr><tr><td>50 Ah or smaller, such as a kayak trolling-motor battery</td><td>Redodo 14.6V 10A</td><td>50 Ah ÷ 10 A = 5 h, at $59.99. {buy:redodo-14-6v-10a-lifepo4-charger}</td></tr><tr><td>200 Ah, or two 100 Ah in parallel</td><td>LiTime 40A or Redodo 40A</td><td>200 Ah ÷ 40 A = 5 h. LiTime costs $12.80 less but recommends indoor use. Redodo adds a 0 V pre-charge. {buy:redodo-14-6v-40a-lifepo4-charger}</td></tr><tr><td>A battery left on the charger for months on a boat or RV</td><td>Victron Blue Smart IP65 12/15, 120 V</td><td>Holds 13.5 V storage instead of sitting at full, IP65, 5-year warranty. Rated for Li-ion batteries of 30–150 Ah.</td></tr><tr><td>A garage that also has lead-acid batteries</td><td>NOCO GENIUS10</td><td>Separate chemistry modes, including 12 V lithium, and a 3-year warranty.</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>Cost per amp: what a LiFePO4 charger's price buys</h2><p>Most of a LiFePO4 refill happens at constant current: in Victron's worked example, 9.5 of the 10 hours are bulk charging. So the amp rating sets your wait, and price per amp shows what that speed costs. Among the 10–20 A chargers that suit a single 100 Ah battery, the Redodo 20A is the cheapest per amp at $4.15. The lowest figure found for a new charger is LiTime's 80 A charger, at $259.99 ÷ 80 A = $3.25 per amp. It runs on 100–120 V AC input only and uses a 120 A Anderson connector, so it suits a large bank. Use it only if your battery's own spec sheet allows 80 A of charge current.</p><p><strong>Charge voltage.</strong> The Redodo and LiTime chargers charge to 14.6 V. The Redodo then shuts off instead of floating. In Li-ion mode the Victron stops at 14.2 V, has no float stage and holds 13.5 V for storage. It also drops temperature compensation in that mode. On a 20 Ah LiFePO4 battery in lithium mode, Auto Median (Chris Perling) measured the NOCO GENIUS10 topping off at about 14.2 V and holding about 13.6 V. The two premium chargers therefore fill a little more gently, while the 14.6 V units fill to the top.</p><p><strong>Waking a battery whose BMS has shut off.</strong> Redodo says its 20 A and 10 A chargers 'can activate lithium battery protected by BMS', and its 40 A has a pre-charge mode that starts from 0 V. LiTime lists 0 V activation on its 20 A. Victron's manual says the Blue Smart IP65 'will automatically reset UVP and start charging'. The NOCO has a manual Force Mode instead, which Auto Median notes 'bypasses battery detection'.</p><p><strong>Heat and cold.</strong> Victron rates the 12/15 for −20 to 50 °C, but gives full rated output only up to 30 °C (86 °F). Its manual says not to charge Li-ion below 0 °C, yet the charger keeps running below freezing, so a cold boat or RV needs a battery that blocks cold charging itself. Redodo's low-temperature 100 Ah battery stops charging below 32 °F and resumes above 41 °F. US buyers need the 120 V Victron model (100–130 VAC input).</p><h2>Not recommended</h2><p>The NOCO GENIUS10 as the only charger for a 100 Ah or larger LiFePO4 battery. At $9.99 per amp it costs 2.4× the Redodo 20A's $4.15 and takes about 10 h to the Redodo's 5 h on 100 Ah. Auto Median measured its lithium top-off at about 14.2 V. It earns its place only if lead-acid batteries share the garage.</p>\n",
 "sources": [('Redodo 14.6V 20A: $82.99, 14.6 V, 20 A, pre-charge/CC/CV then cut-off, BMS activation, 100 Ah to 50% in 2.5 h, 2-year warranty (read 2026-11-08)', 'https://www.redodopower.com/products/redodo-14-6v-20a-lifepo4-battery-charger'), ('Redodo 14.6V 10A: $59.99, 14.6 V, 10 A, BMS activation, 50 Ah to 50% in 2.5 h (read 2026-11-08)', 'https://www.redodopower.com/products/redodo-14-6v-10a-lifepo4-battery-charger'), ('Redodo 14.6V 40A: $179.99, 14.6 V, 40 A, pre-charge from 0 V, 200 Ah in about 5 h (read 2026-11-08)', 'https://www.redodopower.com/products/redodo-14-6v-40a-lifepo4-upgrade-handle-battery-charger'), ('LiTime 12V (14.6V) 20A: $102.99, 14.6 V, 20 A, 0 V activation (read 2026-11-08)', 'https://www.litime.com/products/12v-20a-lifepo4-battery-charger'), ('LiTime 12V (14.6V) 40A: $167.19, 40 A, 100 Ah in 2.5 h and 200 Ah in 5 h, indoor use recommended (read 2026-11-08)', 'https://www.litime.com/products/40a-charger-for-12v-lifepo4-battery'), ('LiTime 12V 80A: $259.99, 100–120 V AC input only, 120 A Anderson (read 2026-11-08)', 'https://www.litime.com/products/litime-14-6v-80a-mountable-lifepo4-battery-charger'), ('Victron Blue Smart IP65 12/15 120 V: Li-ion 14.2 V absorption, no float, 13.5 V storage; 15 A / 4 A; Li-ion battery range 30–150 Ah; full output to 30 °C; 100–130 VAC input (read 2026-11-08)', 'https://www.victronenergy.com/media/pg/Blue_Smart_IP65_Charger_120V_manual/en/technical-specifications---bsc---psc.html'), ('Victron manual: automatic UVP reset for Li-ion, no Li-ion charging below 0 °C, no temperature compensation in Li-ion mode (read 2026-11-08)', 'https://www.victronenergy.com/media/pg/Blue_Smart_IP65_Charger_120V_manual/en/features---bsc---psc.html'), ('Victron Li-ion charge-time example: 100 Ah on 10 A, 9.5 h bulk plus about 0.5 h absorption (read 2026-11-08)', 'https://www.victronenergy.com/media/pg/Blue_Smart_IP65_Charger_120V_manual/en/operation---bsc---psc.html'), ('Victron Blue Smart IP65: 5-year warranty, revives batteries from 0 V (read 2026-11-08)', 'https://www.victronenergy.com/chargers/blue-smart-ip65-charger'), ('Victron Blue Smart IP65 12/15 120 VAC (BPC121531104R): $175.95 (read 2026-11-08)', 'https://www.solar-electric.com/victron-energy-blue-smart-ip65-12-15-120vac-battery-charger.html'), ('NOCO GENIUS10: $99.87 as of 2026-11-08, 10 A, 12 V lithium mode, 3-year warranty, per Clamp & Crank (read 2026-11-08)', 'https://clampandcrank.com/battery-chargers/best-lithium-battery-chargers'), ('NOCO GENIUS10 measured by Auto Median (Chris Perling): about 14.2 V top-off and about 13.6 V hold on a 20 Ah LiFePO4; Force Mode bypasses battery detection (read 2026-11-08)', 'https://automedian.com/noco-genius10-battery-charger-review/'), ('Redodo 12V 100Ah low-temp battery: charging stops below 32 °F and resumes above 41 °F (read 2026-11-08)', 'https://www.redodopower.com/products/redodo-12v-100ah-lithium-marine-batteries')],
 "published": '2026-11-06',
 "checked": '2026-11-08',
 "updated": '2026-11-12'},

