{"slug": 'best-portable-projector-with-screen',
 "question": 'G164 (gap mining daily: projector and screen bundle, 3292 Bing searches / 3 mo, coverage 0.254)',
 "method": 'ab-2026-11', "all_links": True,
 "angle": 'D',
 "searched_as": ['best portable projector and screen bundle 2026 outdoor indoor', 'best portable projector with screen bundle 2026 reviews prices', 'best portable projector with screen included bundle 2026', 'best portable projector with screen included bundle 2026 reviews', 'best portable projectors with screen included bundle 2026', 'best portable projector with included screen bundle 2026'],
 "title": 'Best Portable Projector with Screen (2026): Aurzen EAZZE D1 + 120-inch Screen',
 "h1": 'Best portable projector with screen',
 "desc": 'How bright is each portable projector on its screen? Lumens × gain ÷ area: the Aurzen EAZZE D1 MAX gives about 25.7 ft-L on a 120-inch screen, while battery models dim in Eco mode.',
 "answer": '<p class="lead"><strong>Short answer.</strong> The best portable projector with screen is the Aurzen EAZZE D1 MAX plus Aurzen\'s 120-inch screen, bought as a pair rather than a bundle: 1,000 ANSI lumens light that screen to about 25.7 ft-L, above the 16 ft-L target. Battery models dim: the MoGo 4 measured 151 lumens in Eco.</p>',
 "columns": [('rated', 'Brightness (rated / measured)'), ('battery', 'On battery'), ('ftl', 'On a 120-in, 1.1-gain screen'), ('fit', 'Largest image at 16 ft-L')],
 "rows": [{'slug': 'aurzen-eazze-d1-max-google-tv-projector', 'model': 'Aurzen EAZZE D1 MAX', 'cells': {'rated': '1,000 ANSI lm rated (Aurzen)', 'battery': 'No battery; mains 100–240 V (ProjectorCentral)', 'ftl': '25.7 ft-L', 'fit': '152 in, more than the 120-in screen'}}, {'slug': 'aurzen-eazze-d1-smart-projector', 'model': 'Aurzen EAZZE D1', 'cells': {'rated': '200 ANSI lm rated (ProjectorCentral spec table)', 'battery': 'No battery; mains 100–240 V (ProjectorCentral)', 'ftl': '5.1 ft-L', 'fit': '68 in'}}, {'slug': 'xgimi-mogo-4', 'model': 'XGIMI MoGo 4', 'cells': {'rated': '450 ISO lm rated; 400–404 measured in Performance (ProjectorCentral)', 'battery': 'Up to 2.5 h, rated in Eco (XGIMI); Eco measured 151–154 lm (ProjectorCentral)', 'ftl': '10.4 ft-L in Performance; 3.9 in Eco', 'fit': '97 in in Performance; 59 in in Eco'}}, {'brand': 'Yaber', 'model': 'T2 Plus GTV', 'url': 'https://www.yaber.com/products/t2-plus-google-tv-projector', 'cells': {'price': '$359 (maker, 2026-11-14)', 'rated': '450 ANSI lm as stated by SlashGear; 292 measured (Test-Achats)', 'battery': '2.5 h rated; brightness setting drops from 100 to 60 on battery (SlashGear); Eco measured 202 ANSI lm (Test-Achats)', 'ftl': '7.5 ft-L at 292 lm; 5.2 in Eco', 'fit': '82 in; 68 in in Eco'}}, {'slug': 'nebula-capsule-3-gtv', 'model': 'NEBULA Capsule 3', 'cells': {'rated': '200 ANSI lm rated; 161 measured plugged in (The Hook Up)', 'battery': '2 h 53 min at 112 lm in Eco (The Hook Up)', 'ftl': '4.1 ft-L plugged in; 2.9 in Eco', 'fit': '61 in; 51 in in Eco'}}],
 "after": "\n<h2>What the differences mean</h2><p>Screen brightness in foot-lamberts (ft-L) is the projector's lumens × the screen's gain ÷ the screen's area in square feet. ProjectorCentral gives the SMPTE dark-room target as 16 ft-L, with 12–22 ft-L allowed. Aurzen's 120-inch 16:9 screen covers 120² × 0.0029674 = 42.7 sq ft at 1.1 gain.</p><ul><li>Lumens needed for 16 ft-L on that screen: 16 × 42.7 ÷ 1.1 = 621 lm. Even the 12 ft-L floor needs 466 lm.</li><li>EAZZE D1 MAX: 1,000 × 1.1 ÷ 42.7 = 25.7 ft-L. That is above the 22 ft-L ceiling, so there is headroom for dusk or a porch light. The figure uses Aurzen's rating, not a lab measurement.</li><li>EAZZE D1: 200 × 1.1 ÷ 42.7 = 5.1 ft-L on the full screen. It reaches 16 ft-L at √(200 × 1.1 ÷ 16 ÷ 0.0029674) = 68 in. Use its 50–100% zoom to shrink the picture to about 70 in.</li><li>MoGo 4 in Eco: 151 × 1.1 ÷ 42.7 = 3.9 ft-L, about a quarter of the target.</li><li>Cost on aurzen.com, 2026-11-14: D1 MAX $349.99 + screen $24.99 = $374.98. D1 $149.99 + screen $24.99 = $174.98.</li></ul><table><thead><tr><th>Use</th><th>Fits</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Backyard or living room, full 120-inch picture, outlet or extension cord nearby</td><td>EAZZE D1 MAX {buy:aurzen-eazze-d1-max-google-tv-projector} + 120-inch screen {buy:aurzen-120-inch-portable-projector-screen}</td><td>25.7 ft-L on the whole screen</td></tr><tr><td>Bedroom or tripod setup, picture around 70 in</td><td>EAZZE D1 {buy:aurzen-eazze-d1-smart-projector} on Aurzen's foldable stand</td><td>68 in at 16 ft-L; the stand's 1/4-inch mount lists the D1</td></tr><tr><td>Roku streaming, picture up to 80 in</td><td>Vankyo Performance H500R {buy:vankyo-performance-h500r-roku-tv}</td><td>330 ANSI lm rated by Vankyo (Notebookcheck); Vankyo rates it for 55–80 in; √(330 × 1.1 ÷ 16 ÷ 0.0029674) gives 87 in at 16 ft-L</td></tr><tr><td>No outlet at all</td><td>XGIMI MoGo 4 {buy:xgimi-mogo-4}, picture about 60 in</td><td>In Eco, 59 in at 16 ft-L for about 2.5 h</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>Why battery hours and brightness don't add up</h2><p>XGIMI rates the MoGo 4 for “up to 2.5 hours video playtime” in Eco Mode and notes that leaving Eco shortens playtime. Its 450 ISO lumen figure is measured in Performance or High Power mode. Nikki Kahl at ProjectorCentral measured 400–404 lm in Performance, 258–270 lm in Standard and 151–154 lm in Eco, and Eco lasted about 2.5 h. That means 151 ÷ 404 = 37% of the plugged-in light for the advertised runtime. The same pattern shows up on other battery projectors. Steve Smith at SlashGear found the Yaber T2 Plus drops its brightness setting from 100 to 60 on battery. Test-Achats measured that projector at 292 ANSI lm in normal mode and 202 in Eco. The Hook Up measured the NEBULA Capsule 3 at 161 lm plugged in and 112 lm in Eco, which lasted 2 h 53 min. The rule: take the Eco-mode lumens, then choose the screen size. At 16 ft-L on a 1.1-gain screen, 151 lm fills about 59 in.</p><p>Mounting matters for a grab-and-go setup. Aurzen says the D1 MAX has no 1/4-inch threaded hole and needs a ceiling mount with 4× M5 screws, so outdoors it sits on a table or box, not a tripod. ProjectorCentral lists a 1.28:1 throw ratio. A 120-inch 16:9 image is 104.6 in wide, so the lens sits 1.28 × 104.6 = 134 in (about 11 ft) from the screen. The D1 does fit Aurzen's $39.99 foldable stand, which lists it by name.</p><h2>Not recommended</h2><p>A battery projector on a 120-inch screen. In Eco, the MoGo 4 gives 3.9 ft-L and the Capsule 3 gives 2.9 ft-L on that screen, both under a quarter of the 16 ft-L target. Both are fine at 50–60 in. The same goes for running the EAZZE D1 at the full 120 inches (5.1 ft-L): zoom it down to about 70 in or step up to the D1 MAX.</p>\n",
 "sources": [('SMPTE 16 ft-L target (12–22 allowed); ft-L = lumens × gain ÷ square feet', 'https://www.projectorcentral.com/simple-guide-to-calculating-projector-lumens.htm'), ('Aurzen 120-inch screen: 1.1 gain, 16:9, $24.99 (2026-11-14)', 'https://aurzen.com/products/120-foldable-projector-screen'), ('EAZZE D1 MAX: True 1000 ANSI, $349.99, no 1/4-inch thread, ceiling mount with 4× M5 (2026-11-14)', 'https://aurzen.com/products/eazze-d1-max-google-tv-projector'), ('EAZZE D1 MAX: 1.28:1 throw, 3.7–18.6 ft for 39.8–200 in, 100–240 V input', 'https://www.projectorcentral.com/aurzen-eazze_d1_max.htm'), ('EAZZE D1: 200 ANSI lm (ANSI IT7.228), 1.35:1 throw, 100–240 V input', 'https://www.projectorcentral.com/aurzen-eazze_d1.htm'), ('EAZZE D1: $149.99, 50–100% zoom (2026-11-14)', 'https://aurzen.com/products/eazze-d1-projector'), ('Aurzen Foldable Projector Stand: 1/4-inch mount, lists EAZZE D1, 5.5 lb capacity', 'https://aurzen.com/products/aurzen-foldable-projector-stand'), ('MoGo 4: 2.5 h playtime rated in Eco Mode; 450 ISO lm measured in Performance/High Power', 'https://us.xgimi.com/pages/mogo-4'), ('MoGo 4 measured 400–404 / 258–270 / 151–154 ISO lm by power mode; Eco about 2.5 h', 'https://www.projectorcentral.com/xgimi-mogo-4-1080p-smart-portable-projector-review.htm'), ('Yaber T2 Plus: brightness setting 100 to 60 on battery; 2.5 h rated; 450 ANSI lm stated', 'https://www.slashgear.com/1870982/yaber-t2-plus-projector-review-smart-outdoor-movies-without-cord'), ('Yaber T2 Plus measured 292 ANSI lm normal, 202 Eco', 'https://www.test-achats.be/hightech/projecteurs/comparateur/yaber-t2-plus/325/126009'), ('Yaber T2 Plus GTV $359 at yaber.com (2026-11-14)', 'https://www.yaber.com/products/t2-plus-google-tv-projector'), ('NEBULA Capsule 3 measured 161 lm plugged in, 112 lm Eco, 2 h 53 min', 'https://www.thesmarthomehookup.com/test_install/?p=6317'), ('Vankyo H500R: 330 ANSI lm claimed by Vankyo, 55–80 in image range', 'https://www.notebookcheck.net/Vankyo-launches-new-H500R-affordable-projector-with-Roku-OS-and-330-lumens-brightness.1139060.0.html')],
 "published": '2026-11-06',
 "checked": '2026-11-14',
 "updated": '2026-11-14'},

