# ---------------- G298: solar-inverter-that-works-without-battery (research method ab-2026-11, 2026-11-13) ----------------
{"slug": 'solar-inverter-that-works-without-battery',
 "question": 'G298 (gap mining daily 2026-11-13, research method ab-2026-11: solar inverter that works without battery)',
 "run": 'combo-1113',
 "method": 'ab-2026-11', "all_links": True,
 "angle": 'C',
 "searched_as": ['solar inverter batteryless operation off grid PV only EG4 6000XP Growatt SPF 5000 ES SMA secure power supply specifications', 'official solar inverter batteryless operation grid outage Enphase IQ8 sunlight backup Sol-Ark 15K battery optional EG4 18kPV'],
 "title": 'Solar inverter that works without a battery: which ones keep power on in an outage',
 "h1": 'Solar inverters that work without a battery',
 "desc": 'Which solar inverters run without a battery, and which still power loads in a grid outage: Enphase IQ8 Sunlight Backup, SMA SPS, EG4 18kPV, Sun Gold SPH6548P, Sol-Ark 15K.',
 "answer": '<p class="lead"><strong>Short answer.</strong> A solar inverter that works without a battery in a grid outage: Enphase IQ8 or IQ9 microinverters with Sunlight Backup, which need an IQ System Controller 2/3/3G and at least one IQ Load Controller, then run loads up to 30% of the array\'s AC rating while the sun shines.</p>',
 "columns": [('outage', 'Outage power with no battery'), ('needs', 'What it takes'), ('rated', 'Rated AC output'), ('type', 'System type')],
 "rows": [{'brand': 'Enphase', 'model': 'IQ8 / IQ9 Microinverters with Sunlight Backup (IQ System Controller + IQ Load Controller)', 'url': 'https://enphase.com/homeowners/sunlight-backup-user-guide', 'cells': {'outage': "Yes, in daylight, switching over automatically. Loads up to 30% of the array's AC rating (24 IQ8 = 5.7 kW AC → 1.7 kW), on up to 4 × 240 V or 8 × 120 V circuits (Enphase)", 'needs': "IQ8 or IQ9 micros + IQ System Controller 2/3/3G + at least one IQ Load Controller. IQ6/7 aren't on Enphase's Sunlight Backup list", 'rated': '320 VA continuous per IQ8MC (Northern Arizona Wind & Sun)', 'type': "Grid-tied microinverters. Without Sunlight Backup they 'produce solar energy only when the grid is up' (Enphase)", 'price': '$186.66 per IQ8MC (Northern Arizona Wind & Sun, 2026-11-13) + $2,199.00 IQ System Controller 3 (Signature Solar, 2026-11-13)'}}, {'brand': 'SMA', 'model': 'Sunny Boy 7.0-US (SB7.0-1SP-US-40) with Secure Power Supply', 'url': 'https://www.sma-america.com/newsroom/news-details/sma-expands-residential-portfolio-by-adding-new-sunny-boy-models-with-secure-power-supply', 'cells': {'outage': 'Yes, in daylight: up to 2,000 W from one dedicated outlet, switched on by hand (SMA; OutageMath)', 'needs': "Nothing extra: the outlet is built in. SMA: 'without the need of costly batteries'", 'rated': '7,000 W at 240 V (Northern Arizona Wind & Sun)', 'type': 'Grid-tie string inverter. Discontinued, and so is its -41 replacement (Northern Arizona Wind & Sun)', 'price': '$1,625.48 (Northern Arizona Wind & Sun, 2026-11-13)'}}, {'brand': 'EG4', 'model': '18kPV-12LV Hybrid Inverter', 'url': 'https://eg4electronics.com/categories/inverters/eg4-18kpv-12lv-all-in-one-hybrid-inverter/', 'cells': {'outage': "Yes: with 'No Battery' on, solar supplies loads when the grid fails. EG4 warns this output 'is not stable' (EG4 manual, p. 50)", 'needs': "Turn on 'No Battery' (manual p. 84) or 'PV Grid Off' (p. 50). EG4 suggests adding a battery to keep the backup output stable", 'rated': '12,000 W continuous, 120/240 V split phase (Signature Solar)', 'type': 'Hybrid: grid-tied, grid-assist or fully off-grid (Signature Solar)', 'price': '$3,999.99 (Signature Solar, 2026-11-13)'}}, {'slug': 'sungoldpower-sph6548p-6-5kw-48v-hybrid-inverter', 'model': 'Sun Gold Power SPH6548P 6.5 kW 48 V Split Phase Solar Inverter', 'cells': {'outage': "The listing says it 'supports battery-free' (Sun Gold Power)", 'needs': "Battery 'User Mode' with the battery-free option. Output modes include Solar Priority (Sun Gold Power)", 'rated': '6,500 W rated, 13,000 VA peak, 2 MPPT, 550 VDC max PV Voc (Sun Gold Power)', 'type': "Off-grid all-in-one: 'UL 1741 by ETL for Off Grid Solar System' (Sun Gold Power)"}}, {'brand': 'Sol-Ark', 'model': '15K-2P Hybrid Inverter (SA-15K-2P-N)', 'url': 'https://sol-ark.com/residential-energy-solutions/whole-home-15k-2p-hybrid-inverter/', 'cells': {'outage': 'No: OutageMath lists Sol-Ark among systems that need a battery for any backup', 'needs': "A battery for backup (OutageMath). Batteries in a Flash lists a 'Battery (optional)' output of 12,000 W and a fully grid-tied sell-back mode", 'rated': '15 kW grid output, 13 kW backup for 30 minutes, 24 kW surge (Sol-Ark)', 'type': 'Whole-home hybrid inverter (Sol-Ark)', 'price': '$6,900.00 pre-wired system (Batteries in a Flash, 2026-11-13)'}}],
 "after": "\n<h2>What the differences mean</h2><ul><li><strong>About 71 W of outage load per Enphase microinverter.</strong> 0.30 × 5,700 W ÷ 24 IQ8 = 71 W. Sunlight Backup covers a few essential circuits, not the whole house. Enphase says whole-home backup 'is not supported'.</li><li><strong>Starting a fridge takes about 13 IQ8MC.</strong> OutageMath puts a fridge's start surge at about 1,200 W. 1,200 W ÷ 0.30 = 4,000 W of array AC rating, and 4,000 ÷ 320 VA = 12.5, so 13 microinverters.</li><li><strong>Enphase parts for a roughly 5.7 kW array come to about $5,560 before load controllers.</strong> 18 × $186.66 = $3,359.88 for 18 × 320 VA = 5,760 VA, plus $2,199.00 for the IQ System Controller 3 = $5,558.88. Add IQ Load Controllers (OutageMath estimates $449–$629 each) and labor.</li><li><strong>Cost per rated AC kW:</strong> SPH6548P $1,035 ÷ 6.5 = $159. SMA $1,625.48 ÷ 7 = $232. EG4 $3,999.99 ÷ 12 = $333. Sol-Ark $6,900 ÷ 15 = $460 (a pre-wired system).</li></ul><table><thead><tr><th>Your situation</th><th>Fits</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Grid-tied home, want a few circuits (fridge, lights, Wi-Fi) to switch over automatically during sunny outages</td><td>Enphase IQ8 or IQ9 with Sunlight Backup</td></tr><tr><td>Already own a Sunny Boy with Secure Power Supply and want one outlet for phones or a fridge</td><td>SMA Secure Power Supply (2,000 W, one outlet)</td></tr><tr><td>Want a large hybrid now and a battery later, and can live with unstable solar-only output until then</td><td>EG4 18kPV with 'No Battery' enabled</td></tr><tr><td>Off-grid shed or cabin on a tight budget, battery to follow</td><td>Sun Gold Power SPH6548P</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>Which hardware actually runs without a battery</h2><p>An ordinary grid-tied inverter goes dark in an outage. Under IEEE 1547 it must detect the outage and stop exporting within 2 seconds (5 if the utility extends it), as OutageMath summarizes. To keep running, the inverter has to form its own grid, and something has to cut the house off from the utility lines. Each maker handles this differently.</p><p><strong>Enphase:</strong> On Enphase's storage compatibility page, Sunlight Backup 'is supported with IQ System Controller 2/3/3G, IQ8 or IQ9 Microinverters and IQ Gateway or IQ Combiner', and 'at least one IQ Load Controller is required' to commission it. IQ6/7 microinverters aren't named, so an IQ7 array doesn't qualify. The same page marks IQ System Controller 2 and IQ Combiner 4/4C as end-of-life, so new installs use the 3 or 3G controller. Without this hardware, the matrix says a solar-only system will 'produce solar energy only when the grid is up'. The Solar Lab saw the same thing in testing: its IQ8MC rig with no Sunlight Backup hardware needed 'an active grid reference' and produced about 800 W from 1,460 W of panels with a simulated grid present. Enphase's user guide says that if loads exceed production, the system shuts down and can take up to two minutes to restart. It then brings loads back on 22 seconds apart. One IQ Load Controller covers 2 × 240 V or 4 × 120 V circuits, so the full 4 × 240 V needs two.</p><p><strong>EG4 18kPV:</strong> EG4's manual (p. 84) says 'No Battery' 'can be enabled to use solar power to supply load when the grid fails or load-shedding happens'. On p. 50 it says that when off-grid with no battery, 'the Off-Grid energy is supplied by solar and is not stable', and EG4 suggests installing batteries 'to keep the EPS/UPS output voltage stable'. Use it for light daytime loads until a battery goes in.</p><p><strong>SMA Secure Power Supply:</strong> Northern Arizona Wind &amp; Sun says the outlet has power 'as long as the sun is shining', up to 2,000 W. OutageMath says you switch it on by hand. Both the -40 and -41 Sunny Boy 7.0 are now listed as discontinued, so this suits existing owners more than new buyers.</p><p><strong>Sun Gold Power SPH6548P:</strong> None of these is a product we list except this one. It is the lowest-priced all-in-one here whose maker listing says it 'supports battery-free' operation, at $159 per rated kW. It is listed for off-grid systems, not for exporting to the grid. Sun Gold's listing doesn't give a wattage for loads run from panels alone, so ask Sun Gold for the battery-free load limit before you count on it for outage power. {buy:sungoldpower-sph6548p-6-5kw-48v-hybrid-inverter}</p><h2>Not recommended</h2><p><strong>Sol-Ark 15K-2P for outage power without a battery.</strong> OutageMath lists Sol-Ark among systems that need a battery to back anything up, so the 13 kW backup rating on Sol-Ark's page doesn't apply without one. The Solar Lab measured the 15K drawing 97 W idle in standby. If it draws that all day and night, 97 W × 8,760 h = about 850 kWh a year. At $6,900 for the pre-wired system, it only makes sense if you're buying the battery too.</p>\n",
 "sources": [('Enphase Sunlight Backup: loads at or below 30% of IQ8 AC rating (24 IQ8 = 5.7 kW AC), 4 × 240 V or 8 × 120 V circuits, up to 2-minute restart, 22 s load restore, whole-home not supported (read 2026-11-13)', 'https://enphase.com/homeowners/sunlight-backup-user-guide'), ('Enphase compatibility: Sunlight Backup with IQ System Controller 2/3/3G + IQ8 or IQ9, at least one IQ Load Controller; IQ6/7 not named for Sunlight Backup; IQ System Controller 2, IQ Combiner 4/4C marked EOL; solar-only produces only when the grid is up (read 2026-11-13)', 'https://enphase.com/installers/storage/compatibility'), ("EG4 18kPV manual: 'No Battery' setting (p. 84); 'PV Grid Off' and 'not stable' warning (p. 50) (read 2026-11-13)", 'https://www.manualslib.com/manual/3312143/Eg4-18kpv.html?page=84'), ('EG4 18kPV-12LV price $3,999.99, 12,000 W continuous, grid-tied/grid-assist/off-grid (read 2026-11-13)', 'https://signaturesolar.com/eg4-18kpv-hybrid-inverter-all-in-one-solar-inverter-eg4-18kpv-12lv/'), ('Enphase IQ8MC-72-M-US price $186.66, 320 VA continuous (read 2026-11-13)', 'https://www.solar-electric.com/enphase-iq8mc-72-m-us-micro-inverter.html'), ('Enphase IQ System Controller 3 price $2,199.00 (read 2026-11-13)', 'https://signaturesolar.com/enphase-iq-system-controller-3/'), ('SMA Sunny Boy 7.0-US -40 price $1,625.48, 7,000 W, discontinued, SPS outlet powered while the sun shines (read 2026-11-13)', 'https://www.solar-electric.com/sma-sunny-boy-sb7-0-us-grid-tie-inverter.html'), ("SMA Sunny Boy 7.0-1SP-US-41: 'This product has been discontinued', end of life (read 2026-11-13)", 'https://www.solar-electric.com/sma-sunny-boy-7-0-1sp-us-41-grid-tie-inverter.html'), ("SMA: Secure Power Supply up to 2,000 W in an outage 'without the need of costly batteries' (SMA newsroom, 2016-08-09; read 2026-11-13)", 'https://www.sma-america.com/newsroom/news-details/sma-expands-residential-portfolio-by-adding-new-sunny-boy-models-with-secure-power-supply'), ("Sun Gold Power SPH6548P price $1,035.00, 'supports battery-free', 6,500 W rated, 13,000 VA peak, UL 1741 for off-grid (read 2026-11-13)", 'https://sungoldpower.com/products/6500w-48v-solar-charge-inverter-parallel-wifi-monitor'), ('Sol-Ark 15K-2P: 15 kW grid, 13 kW backup for 30 min, 24 kW surge (read 2026-11-13)', 'https://sol-ark.com/residential-energy-solutions/whole-home-15k-2p-hybrid-inverter/'), ("Sol-Ark 15K-2P pre-wired system price $6,900.00, 'Battery (optional)' output 12,000 W, fully grid-tied sell-back mode (read 2026-11-13)", 'https://www.batteriesinaflash.com/solar/sol-ark-sa-15k-2p-n-15-0kw-battery-based-inverter'), ('OutageMath: Sol-Ark needs a battery for backup, SMA SPS switched on by hand, IEEE 1547 2 s shutdown, fridge 1,200 W start, IQ Load Controller $449–$629 (updated 2026-11-10; read 2026-11-13)', 'https://www.outagemath.com/guides/solar-without-battery-power-outage/'), ('The Solar Lab: Sol-Ark 15K measured 97 W idle in standby (read 2026-11-13)', 'https://www.thesolarlab.com/review/sol-ark-15k-hybrid-inverter-review'), ('The Solar Lab: IQ8MC rig needed an active grid reference, about 800 W from 1,460 W of panels (read 2026-11-13)', 'https://www.thesolarlab.com/review/enphase-iq8mc-microinverter')],
 "published": '2026-11-13',
 "checked": '2026-11-13',
 "updated": '2026-11-17'},

