# ---------------- best-iphone-17-case-with-card-holder (research method ab-2026-11, 2026-11-17) ----------------
{"slug": 'best-iphone-17-case-with-card-holder',
 "question": 'G315 (brand page for Smartish: iphone 17 case with card holder)',
 "method": 'ab-2026-11', "all_links": True,
 "angle": 'B',
 "searched_as": ['iPhone 17 wallet case cards remain inserted MagSafe wireless charging compatible 2026', 'iPhone 17 case built in card holder supports MagSafe wireless charging without removing cards 2026'],
 "title": 'Best iPhone 17 Case with Card Holder (2026): Wallet Slayer vs Folio vs MagSafe Wallet',
 "h1": 'Best iPhone 17 case with card holder',
 "desc": "Which iPhone 17 card cases still charge on MagSafe: a front-flap folio keeps the cards off the charger, while 3 cards in a rear slot stack 2.28 mm, past Apple's 2.1 mm case limit. Prices checked 2026-11-17.",
 "answer": '<p class="lead"><strong>Short answer.</strong> The best iPhone 17 case with a card holder that still works with MagSafe charging is the Nomad Modern Leather Folio: its 3 cards sit in the front flap, not behind the phone. Three cards in a rear slot stack 2.28 mm, over Apple\'s 2.1 mm MagSafe case limit, so they come out to charge.</p>',
 "columns": [('cards', 'Cards held'), ('where', 'Where the cards sit'), ('stack', 'Card stack between phone and charger'), ('magsafe', 'MagSafe charging with cards loaded')],
 "rows": [{'brand': 'Nomad', 'model': 'Modern Leather Folio (iPhone 17)', 'url': 'https://nomadgoods.com/products/modern-leather-folio-black-iphone-17', 'cells': {'cards': '3 cards + 1 cash slot (Nomad)', 'where': 'Inside the fold-over front flap (Nomads Nation)', 'stack': '0 mm: the charger attaches to the back shell (Nomad photo)', 'magsafe': "Yes by Apple's rule, because the cards aren't between the phone and the charger. Nomad lists 'MagSafe & Qi2 charging compatible'", 'price': '$74 (maker, 2026-11-17)'}}, {'slug': 'smartish-gripmunk-magsafe-iphone-17', 'model': 'Smartish Gripmunk with MagSafe (iPhone 17) + a MagSafe wallet', 'cells': {'cards': 'None in the case; 4 in an ESR Geo Wallet Boost', 'where': 'In the snap-on wallet, over the MagSafe ring', 'stack': '3.04 mm with the wallet on (4 × 0.76); 0 mm with it off', 'magsafe': "Only with the wallet off. Smartish says its magnets 'stay fully wireless-charging compatible'"}}, {'slug': 'esr-geo-wallet-boost-halolock', 'model': 'ESR Geo Wallet Boost (HaloLock), Find My', 'cells': {'cards': '4 cards + 3 cash (ESR)', 'where': 'Snaps onto the back, over the MagSafe ring', 'stack': 'Up to 3.04 mm (4 × 0.76)', 'magsafe': 'No: Apple says to remove it before charging'}}, {'slug': 'smartish-wallet-slayer-vol-1-iphone-17', 'model': 'Smartish Wallet Slayer Vol. 1 (iPhone 17)', 'cells': {'cards': '1 to 4 cards + cash (Smartish)', 'where': 'Side-loading slot in the back', 'stack': '0.76 to 3.04 mm', 'magsafe': "No: 'Cable charging only, not MagSafe compatible' (Smartish)"}}, {'brand': 'Scooch', 'model': 'Wingmate Hidden Wallet Phone Case (Black)', 'url': 'https://scooch.com/products/wingmate-black', 'cells': {'cards': '3 cards + cash, or up to 4 slim cards (Scooch)', 'where': 'Bottom-loading compartment in the back', 'stack': '2.28 mm with 3 cards; up to 3.04 mm with 4 slim cards', 'magsafe': "No: 'cannot charge wirelessly or with MagSafe while the case is on' (Scooch)", 'price': '$29.99 (maker, 2026-11-17)'}}],
 "after": '\n<h2>What the differences mean</h2><ul><li><strong>Cards behind the phone:</strong> a standard bank card is 0.76 mm thick (ISO/IEC 7810). So 3 cards = 3 × 0.76 = 2.28 mm, and 4 cards = 4 × 0.76 = 3.04 mm. Apple\'s limit for a whole MagSafe case is 2.1 mm, as MacRumors reported from Apple\'s 2020 accessory guidelines. Three cards alone exceed it by 2.28 − 2.1 = 0.18 mm, before the case\'s own back is counted.</li><li><strong>Nomad per card:</strong> $74 / 3 slots = $24.67 for each card that can stay in while the phone sits on a MagSafe charger. That $74 is a 25%-off sale; the list price is $99.</li><li><strong>Folio vs case plus MagSafe wallet:</strong> Gripmunk with MagSafe $19.99 + ESR Geo Wallet Boost $36.99 = $56.98. The folio costs $74 − $56.98 = $17.02 more, and you don\'t have to pull a wallet off every time you charge.</li><li><strong>Folio vs Wallet Slayer Vol. 1:</strong> $74 − $29.99 = $44.01 more to keep MagSafe charging with the cards in.</li><li><strong>What cable-only charging costs in speed:</strong> ChargerLAB measured the iPhone 17 peaking at 29 W on Apple\'s MagSafe Charger and 27–28 W over USB-C. That is 29 − 28 = 1 W to 29 − 27 = 2 W of peak given up.</li></ul><table><thead><tr><th>If you…</th><th>Pick</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>want the cards to stay in while the phone sits on a MagSafe charger</td><td>Nomad Modern Leather Folio</td><td>3 cards in the front flap, nothing between the back and the charger</td></tr><tr><td>charge on MagSafe and don\'t mind pulling a wallet off first</td><td>Smartish Gripmunk with MagSafe + ESR Geo Wallet Boost</td><td>4 cards plus Find My tracking; charges once the wallet is off</td></tr><tr><td>charge by cable anyway and want a one-piece card case</td><td>Smartish Wallet Slayer Vol. 1</td><td>1 to 4 cards in the back; gives up only 1–2 W of peak speed</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>Why where the cards sit decides MagSafe charging</h2><p>Apple\'s MagSafe Charger page says: "Don\'t place credit cards, security badges, passports, or key fobs between your iPhone and MagSafe Charger," because this might damage magnetic strips or RFID chips. For cases that hold cards, Apple says to remove them before charging or make sure they aren\'t between the back of your device and the charger. A case\'s "MagSafe" label doesn\'t settle it. What settles it is whether the cards sit on the charger\'s side of the phone.</p><p><strong>Folio, cards on the screen side.</strong> Nomads Nation\'s review (Aaron Radcliffe) describes the folio\'s "wallet storage layout built directly into the leather flap". Nomad\'s own photo shows a MagSafe charger attached to the back of the closed folio, and Nomad lists it as "MagSafe & Qi2 charging compatible" with 8 ft drop protection. Nomad doesn\'t say in words that charging works with the cards loaded. The design meets Apple\'s condition because the cards fold over the screen, not onto the coil. Nomads Nation does note that "the magnetic connection is slightly weaker due to the leather layers". Nomad sells a separate folio for each iPhone model, so choose the iPhone 17 one: <a href="https://nomadgoods.com/products/modern-leather-folio-black-iphone-17">Nomad Modern Leather Folio for iPhone 17</a>.</p><p><strong>Case plus snap-on wallet, cards on the coil.</strong> Smartish says the magnets in its Gripmunk with MagSafe line "stay fully wireless-charging compatible" ({buy:smartish-gripmunk-magsafe-iphone-17}). The ESR Geo Wallet Boost holds 4 cards and 3 bills with 1,800 g of magnetic hold, but it sits exactly where the charger goes, so it comes off before charging ({buy:esr-geo-wallet-boost-halolock}).</p><p><strong>Rear-slot cases, cards in the path.</strong> Smartish describes the Wallet Slayer Vol. 1 line\'s slot as holding 1 to 4 cards and states "Cable charging only, not MagSafe compatible" ({buy:smartish-wallet-slayer-vol-1-iphone-17}). Thickness behind the phone costs watts even where charging still runs. Maplee-Tech, an accessory seller citing unnamed engineers, measured an iPhone 17 at 30.14 W wireless with no case and 21.98 W through a 3.05 mm case: 21.98 / 30.14 = 0.73, about 27% less. 3.05 mm is roughly the thickness of four cards.</p><h2>Not recommended</h2><p><strong>Scooch Wingmate, if you want MagSafe charging.</strong> Scooch sells a MagSafe ring for it, but its own help page says "Wingmate cannot charge wirelessly or with MagSafe while the case is on" and "The ring does not enable wireless charging through Wingmate." Its back compartment holds 3 cards plus cash, or up to 4 slim cards, and it is drop-tested to 10 ft, which makes it fine if you charge by cable. Check Scooch\'s model selector for an iPhone 17 version before ordering.</p>\n',
 "sources": [("Apple's rule: no cards between the iPhone and the MagSafe Charger; remove them or keep them off the back", 'https://support.apple.com/en-us/HT211829'), ("Apple's 2.1 mm maximum thickness for MagSafe cases (MacRumors, 2020)", 'https://www.macrumors.com/2020/11/02/apple-magsafe-design-guidelines-accessory-makers'), ('Bank card thickness 0.76 mm (ISO/IEC 7810)', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO/IEC_7810'), ('Nomad folio: $74 (list $99), 3 card + 1 cash slot, MagSafe & Qi2 compatible, 8 ft drop, charger-on-back photo', 'https://nomadgoods.com/products/modern-leather-folio-black-iphone-17'), ('Nomad folio card slots built into the flap; weaker MagSafe hold (Nomads Nation, Aaron Radcliffe)', 'https://nomadsnation.com/nomad-modern-leather-folio-review/'), ('Wallet Slayer Vol. 1 for iPhone 17: $29.99 on smartish.com', 'https://www.smartish.com/products/wallet-slayer-vol-1-card-case-for-iphone-17'), ("Wallet Slayer Vol. 1 line: 1 to 4 cards, 'Cable charging only, not MagSafe compatible'", 'https://www.smartish.com/products/wallet-slayer-vol-1-card-case-for-iphone-duo'), ('Gripmunk with MagSafe for iPhone 17: $19.99', 'https://www.smartish.com/products/gripmunk-with-magsafe-slim-case-for-iphone-17'), ("Gripmunk with MagSafe magnets 'stay fully wireless-charging compatible'", 'https://www.smartish.com/products/gripmunk-with-magsafe-slim-case-for-iphone-18-pro'), ('ESR Geo Wallet Boost: $36.99, 4 cards + 3 cash, 1,800 g hold, works on MagSafe cases', 'https://www.esrgear.com/products/geo-wallet-boost-halolock'), ("Scooch Wingmate: no wireless or MagSafe charging with the case on; the ring doesn't enable it", 'https://scooch.com/pages/wingmate-info'), ('Scooch Wingmate: $29.99 Black, 3 cards + cash or 4 slim cards, 10-foot drop tested', 'https://scooch.com/products/wingmate-black'), ('iPhone 17 peaks: 29 W on MagSafe, 27–28 W over USB-C (ChargerLAB via MacRumors)', 'https://www.macrumors.com/2025/09/26/iphone-17-usb-c-charging-speed-test/'), ('iPhone 17 wireless output 30.14 W with no case vs 21.98 W through a 3.05 mm case (Maplee-Tech)', 'https://maplee-tech.com/en/iphone-17-magsafe-case-charging-thickness-test-3/')],
 "published": '2026-11-14',
 "checked": '2026-11-17',
 "updated": '2026-11-17'},

