# ---------------- best-replacement-dvr-for-security-cameras (research method ab-2026-11, 2026-11-17) ----------------
{"slug": 'best-replacement-dvr-for-security-cameras',
 "question": 'G319 (brand page for ZOSI: replacement dvr for security cameras)',
 "method": 'ab-2026-11', "all_links": True,
 "angle": 'D',
 "searched_as": ['2026 Dahua XVR 8 channel pentabrid CVBS TVI AHD CVI specifications Hikvision DVR analog compatibility', 'Dahua XVR 8 channel pentabrid CVI TVI AHD CVBS official specifications Hikvision iDS 7208HQHI ANNKE DVR compatibility'],
 "title": 'Best Replacement DVR for Security Cameras (2026): Keep Your Coax Cameras',
 "h1": 'Best replacement DVR for security cameras',
 "desc": 'Replacing a dead DVR but keeping your coax cameras? Match their format (CVI, TVI, AHD, CVBS) and their power. The ANNKE DR85 ($79.99, 8 BNC) suits most homes. Cameras powered through the coax need a PoC XVR.',
 "answer": '<p class="lead"><strong>Short answer.</strong> Best replacement DVR for my existing analog security cameras? One that reads their format (CVI, TVI, AHD or CVBS) and matches their power: if the coax alone powers them, buy a PoC DVR; Dahua XVR5108H-I3-8P powers HDCVI PoC cameras. Otherwise: ANNKE DR85, $79.99, 8 channels.</p>',
 "columns": [('bnc', 'Camera inputs'), ('formats', 'Coax formats it reads'), ('top', 'Top coax camera it records'), ('alerts', 'Alerts')],
 "rows": [{'brand': 'ANNKE', 'model': 'DR85', 'url': 'https://www.annke.com/products/dr85', 'cells': {'bnc': '8 BNC + 2 IP', 'formats': 'TVI, AHD, CVI, CVBS', 'top': "3K TVI; 4MP AHD and CVI; records at '3K Lite'", 'alerts': "Human and vehicle detection (ANNKE's title)", 'price': '$79.99 (maker, 2026-11-17)'}}, {'slug': 'zosi-zr08vma-8-channel-1080p-dvr', 'model': 'ZOSI ZR08VMA', 'cells': {'bnc': '8 BNC, no IP channels', 'formats': 'Analog (CVBS), TVI, CVI, AHD', 'top': '1080p; 3MP, 4MP and 5MP at 12.5 fps', 'alerts': 'Motion zones, push and email alerts'}}, {'slug': 'zosi-zr16fk-16-channel-1080p-dvr', 'model': 'ZOSI ZR16FK', 'cells': {'bnc': '16 BNC', 'formats': '4-in-1 HD-TVI DVR (ZOSI listing)', 'top': '1080p', 'alerts': 'Motion zones, push and email alerts'}}, {'brand': 'ANNKE', 'model': 'DR88', 'url': 'https://www.annke.com/products/dr88', 'cells': {'bnc': '8 BNC + 4 IP', 'formats': "5-in-1 hybrid (ANNKE's title)", 'top': '4K TVI', 'alerts': 'Motion-zone alerts', 'price': '$99.99 (maker, 2026-11-17)'}}, {'brand': 'Dahua', 'model': 'XVR5108H-I3-8P (PoC)', 'url': 'https://www.dahuasecurity.com/products/hdcvi-products/hdcvi-recorders/poc-series/5m-n-1080p-series/xvr5108h-i3-8p', 'cells': {'bnc': '8 BNC, each powering HDCVI PoC cameras; 4 IP', 'formats': 'CVI, TVI, AHD, CVBS auto-detect', 'top': '5MP at 20 fps (TVI, AHD) or 25 fps (CVI); 1080p at 25/30 fps', 'alerts': 'SMD and face detection (off once IP extension is on)', 'price': 'Dahua lists no price on its page'}}, {'brand': 'Viewtron', 'model': 'VT-DVR-8', 'url': 'https://cctvcamerapros.com/security-camera-DVR-p/vt-dvr-8.htm', 'cells': {'bnc': '8 BNC + 8 IP', 'formats': 'CVBS (CIF, D1, 960H), AHD, TVI, CVI', 'top': '4K at 7–8 fps (the page gives both); 1080p at 30 fps', 'alerts': 'Motion; the FAQ says no built-in human detection', 'price': '$799.99 (maker, 2026-11-17)'}}, {'brand': 'Dahua', 'model': 'XVR7208A-4K-I3', 'url': 'https://www.dahuasecurity.com/products/HDCVI-Recorders/4K-series/XVR7208A-4K-I3', 'cells': {'bnc': '8 BNC + 8 IP (16 with analog channels converted)', 'formats': 'CVI, TVI, AHD, CVBS auto-detect', 'top': '4K: CVI at 25/30 fps, TVI and AHD at 15 fps', 'alerts': 'SMD, perimeter, face recognition on 2 channels (off once IP extension is on)', 'price': 'Dahua lists no price on its page'}}],
 "after": "\n<h2>What the differences mean</h2><ul><li><strong>Cost per camera, 8 cameras:</strong> ANNKE DR85 $79.99 ÷ 8 = $10.00; ZOSI ZR08VMA $69.99 (no-drive option) ÷ 8 = $8.75; Viewtron VT-DVR-8 $799.99 ÷ 8 = $100.00.</li><li><strong>Cost per camera, 16 cameras:</strong> ZOSI ZR16FK $99.99 ÷ 16 = $6.25, against ANNKE's DR165 at $129.99 ÷ 16 = $8.12.</li><li><strong>Adding a drive:</strong> the DR85 plus ANNKE's cheapest surveillance drive costs $79.99 + $89.99 = $169.98. ANNKE's 8-channel 3K Lite bundle with a 2 TB drive costs $209.99.</li><li><strong>Frames at 4K over coax:</strong> Viewtron records 4K coax cameras at 7 fps and 1080p at 30 fps, so 30 ÷ 7 ≈ 4.3 times fewer frames at 4K. Dahua's XVR7208A-4K-I3 records TVI and AHD 4K at 15 fps. It reaches 30 fps at 4K only on channels 1 and 5, only with CVI cameras, and only with Encode Enhancement on.</li><li><strong>How long recordings last:</strong> the XVR7208A-4K-I3 takes 2 × 16 TB = 32 TB. Eight channels at its 8,192 kbps maximum write 707.8 GB a day, so the drives hold 32,000 ÷ 707.8 ≈ 45 days. The DR88 has one bay of up to 8 TB, which is 1 TB per camera.</li></ul><table><thead><tr><th>Your cameras</th><th>Buy</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Up to 8, on their own 12 V supply, from old CVBS up to 3K TVI</td><td>ANNKE DR85</td></tr><tr><td>Up to 8, 1080p, lowest price, no person detection needed</td><td>ZOSI ZR08VMA {buy:zosi-zr08vma-8-channel-1080p-dvr}</td></tr><tr><td>9 to 16 cameras on their own supply</td><td>ZOSI ZR16FK {buy:zosi-zr16fk-16-channel-1080p-dvr}</td></tr><tr><td>4K TVI coax cameras</td><td>ANNKE DR88</td></tr><tr><td>A single coax to each camera with no power at the camera end, Dahua HDCVI PoC cameras</td><td>Dahua XVR5108H-I3-8P</td></tr><tr><td>Coax PTZ domes, or an NDAA-compliant recorder required</td><td>Viewtron VT-DVR-8 (UTC PTZ control over RG59)</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>Check how your cameras get power before you swap the DVR</h2><p>Matching the video format is only half the job. The other half is power. Look at a camera's cable where it reaches the camera.</p><ul><li><strong>A 12 V adapter, a 1-to-4 splitter, or Siamese cable (coax with a power pair beside it):</strong> the cameras have their own power, and any hybrid DVR above will work. ZOSI's support page tells owners with video loss to check the cameras' power supply and 1-to-4 power splitter cable, and to test each camera on another working 12 V supply. The ZR16FK ships with a 12 V / 2000 mA supply for the recorder itself. Viewtron pairs its DVR with RG59 Siamese cable that 'runs both the video and power'.</li><li><strong>One coax and nothing else:</strong> the old DVR was sending power up the coax (PoC). An ordinary hybrid DVR leaves those cameras unpowered. Dahua's XVR7208A-4K-I3 runs on a 12 VDC 5 A input, draws under 15 W without drives, and lists no camera power. Dahua's XVR5108H-I3-8P has an '8-ch HDCVI PoC AT&amp;AF Camera Power Supply' fed by 53 VDC at 1.812 A (53 × 1.812 ≈ 96 W in). The only cameras it names as powered are HDCVI PoC models. An older Dahua PoC model, the XVR5108H-4KL-X-8P, shows the limits of this design: 48 W in total, enough for 8 AF cameras (48 ÷ 8 = 6 W each) or 4 AT cameras (12 W each), with no balun or twisted-pair runs. If your PoC cameras are another brand, add a 12 V supply at each camera instead.</li><li><strong>Long runs:</strong> Mammoth Security's tests got HD-CVI and HD-TVI to about 1,000 ft on RG-59, against the 'over 1,500 ft' makers claim.</li></ul><h2>Not recommended</h2><p>The <strong>Dahua XVR7208A-4K-I3</strong> is a poor replacement for most home systems. It cannot power cameras that ran on PoC. Its '4K at 30 fps' applies only to channels 1 and 5, with CVI cameras and Encode Enhancement on, and TVI and AHD cameras record 4K at 15 fps. Dahua's page gives no price. The FCC's Covered List includes Dahua Technology and Hikvision, and FCC 25-71 lets the FCC bar future imports and sales of their equipment. If your cameras are 1080p or older CVBS, a 4K recorder will not make their picture any sharper.</p>\n",
 "sources": [('ANNKE DR85 price $79.99, 8 BNC TVI/AHD/CVI/CVBS + 2 IP, 3K TVI and 4MP AHD/CVI, human and vehicle detection (read 2026-11-17)', 'https://www.annke.com/products/dr85'), ('ANNKE DR88 price $99.99, 8 BNC + 4 IP, 4K TVI, motion-zone alerts, 1 bay up to 8 TB (read 2026-11-17)', 'https://www.annke.com/products/dr88'), ('ANNKE DR165 price $129.99, 16 BNC + 2 IP (read 2026-11-17)', 'https://www.annke.com/products/dr165'), ('ANNKE surveillance drives from $89.99; 3K Lite 8CH bundle with 2 TB drive $209.99 (read 2026-11-17)', 'https://www.annke.com/products/b086kq7wxw'), ('ZOSI ZR08VMA from $69.99, analog/TVI/CVI/AHD, 3MP to 5MP at 12.5 fps, motion alerts (read 2026-11-17)', 'https://www.zositech.com/products/8-channel-1080p-dvr-for-tvi-cvi-ahd-analog-security-camera'), ('ZOSI ZR16FK from $99.99, 16 channels at 1080p, 12 V / 2000 mA DVR supply in the box (read 2026-11-17)', 'https://www.zositech.com/products/16ch-1080p-tvi-cvi-ahd-analog-4-in-1-security-dvr-easy-remote-view'), ("ZOSI video-loss support: check the cameras' power supply and 1-to-4 power splitter cable, test with another 12 V supply (read 2026-11-17)", 'https://supports.zositech.com/hc/en-us/articles/234712307-You-got-Video-Loss-on-one-channel-or-all-channels'), ('Viewtron VT-DVR-8: $799.99, CVBS at CIF/D1/960H, 7 fps at 4K, 30 fps at 1080p, UTC PTZ, Siamese RG59, NDAA, 2 × 12 TB bays (read 2026-11-17)', 'https://cctvcamerapros.com/security-camera-DVR-p/vt-dvr-8.htm'), ('Dahua XVR7208A-4K-I3: frame rate per format, 4K at 30 fps on channels 1 and 5 only, 2 × 16 TB, 8,192 kbps max, 12 VDC 5 A, no price (read 2026-11-17)', 'https://www.dahuasecurity.com/products/HDCVI-Recorders/4K-series/XVR7208A-4K-I3'), ('Dahua XVR5108H-I3-8P: 8-ch HDCVI PoC AT&AF camera power, 53 VDC 1.812 A, resolution per format, 4 + 8 IP (read 2026-11-17)', 'https://www.dahuasecurity.com/products/hdcvi-products/hdcvi-recorders/poc-series/5m-n-1080p-series/xvr5108h-i3-8p'), ('Dahua XVR5108H-4KL-X-8P: 48 W PoC budget, 8 AF or 4 AT cameras, no balun or UTP (read 2026-11-17)', 'https://www.dahuasecurity.com/de/products/All-Products/HDCVI-Recorders/PoC-Series/1-HDD/XVR5108H-4KL-X-8P'), ("Mammoth Security tests: HD-CVI and HD-TVI reach about 1,000 ft on RG-59 against a claimed 'over 1,500' ft (read 2026-11-17)", 'https://mammothsecurity.com/blog/ip-vs-analog-cameras'), ('FCC Covered List includes Hikvision and Dahua; FCC 25-71 import and marketing limits (read 2026-11-17)', 'https://docs.fcc.gov/public/attachments/DA-26-48A1.txt')],
 "published": '2026-11-14',
 "checked": '2026-11-17',
 "updated": '2026-11-17'},

