# ---------------- G334: quietest-enclosed-3d-printer-for-an-apartment (research method ab-2026-11, 2026-11-16) ----------------
{"slug": 'quietest-enclosed-3d-printer-for-an-apartment',
 "question": 'G334 (gap mining daily 2026-11-16, research method ab-2026-11: which enclosed 3d printer is the quietest for an apartment)',
 "run": 'bluetti-1115',
 "buy_by_name": True,
 "method": 'ab-2026-11',
 "angle": 'E',
 "searched_as": ['2026 quietest enclosed 3d printer noise measured decibels Prusa CORE One Bambu P1S QIDI Q2 reviews', 'quietest enclosed 3d printer measured noise dBA apartment Bambu P1S QIDI Q1 Pro H2S P2S reviews'],
 "title": 'Which Enclosed 3D Printer Is the Quietest for an Apartment? Measured Noise',
 "h1": 'Which enclosed 3D printer is the quietest for an apartment',
 "desc": "Measured noise for enclosed 3D printers: dB while printing from named testers, with distance, mode and date, next to each maker's own quiet-mode figure.",
 "answer": '<p class="lead"><strong>Short answer.</strong> The quietest enclosed 3D printer for an apartment, on measured noise, is the Elegoo Centauri Carbon 2: Notebookcheck measured 44–47 dB while printing. The Anycubic Kobra S1, rated 44 dB by Anycubic, measured 59.6 dB(A) at igor\'sLAB.</p>',
 "columns": [('measured', 'Measured while printing (tester, date)'), ('conditions', 'Distance and mode of that reading'), ('maker', "Maker's own figure and its conditions"), ('other', 'Other readings (idle, add-ons, same-test gaps)')],
 "rows": [{'brand': 'Elegoo', 'model': 'Centauri Carbon 2', 'url': 'https://us.elegoo.com/products/centauri-carbon-2', 'cells': {'measured': '44–47 dB average, peaks to 54 dB (Notebookcheck, Vineet Washington, review 2026-03-02, read 2026-11-16)', 'conditions': 'Distance, meter and print mode not stated', 'maker': '45 dB: Elegoo Lab, Elegoo PLA, Silent Mode, auxiliary part-cooling fan off; no distance given (Elegoo, read 2026-11-16)', 'other': 'A mild, constant beep while idle (Notebookcheck)', 'price': '$349 (maker, 2026-11-16)'}}, {'brand': 'Anycubic', 'model': 'Kobra S1 (ACE 2 Pro Combo)', 'url': 'https://store.anycubic.com/products/kobra-s1-ace-2-pro-combo-3d-printer', 'cells': {'measured': "59.6 dB(A) while printing (igor'sLAB, Tim Kutzner, 2025-04-14, read 2026-11-16)", 'conditions': 'Distance and print mode not stated; tested as the Kobra S1 Combo', 'maker': '≤44 dB Quiet mode, ≤46 dB Standard mode, at 1 m from the front (Anycubic, read 2026-11-16)', 'other': "Bundled ACE 2 Pro rated 48 dB printing with the door closed, 55 dB while drying, at 1 m (Anycubic). No fans audible at idle (igor'sLAB)", 'price': '$499 (maker, 2026-11-16)'}, 'asin': 'B0GWDCM8NR'}, {'brand': 'Bambu Lab', 'model': 'P2S', 'url': 'https://us.store.bambulab.com/products/p2s', 'cells': {'measured': '65 dB in a 600-hour three-printer test (3D Printed Decor, as reported by StarterBench, read 2026-11-16)', 'conditions': 'Distance and print mode not stated', 'maker': 'Below 50 dB in Silent Mode, tested at 1 m (Bambu Lab wiki, read 2026-11-16)', 'other': '7 dB quieter than the P1S in the same 3D Printed Decor test (arithmetic)', 'price': '$449 (maker, 2026-11-16)'}, 'asin': 'B0FT7ZLSSC'}, {'slug': 'qidi-q2', 'model': 'QIDI Q2', 'cells': {'measured': '56 dB in normal use (androidpctv, review 2025-08-28, read 2026-11-16)', 'conditions': 'Distance and print mode not stated', 'maker': "QIDI's product page gives no dB figure (QIDI, read 2026-11-16)", 'other': '65 dB with the QIDI Box multi-color unit attached (androidpctv)'}}, {'slug': 'flashforge-adventurer-5m-pro', 'model': 'Flashforge Adventurer 5M Pro', 'cells': {'measured': "No named reading of the 5M Pro itself. The open-frame Adventurer 5M measured 62.3 dB(A) printing (igor'sLAB, Tim Kutzner, 2025-02-27, read 2026-11-16)", 'conditions': "Distance not stated; igor'sLAB traced most of the 5M's noise to its small 3010 hotend fan", 'maker': '50 dB in low-noise mode, 55 dB standard; no distance given (Flashforge, read 2026-11-16)', 'other': "Adventurer 5M: 41.1 dB(A) idle, 54.8 dB(A) with only the hotend fan running (igor'sLAB)"}}, {'brand': 'Bambu Lab', 'model': 'P1S', 'url': 'https://us.store.bambulab.com/products/p1s', 'cells': {'measured': "64.7 dB(A) printing (igor'sLAB, Tim Kutzner, 2023-10-12, read 2026-11-16)", 'conditions': 'About 40 cm from the closed front, while printing', 'maker': "Bambu's store page gives no dB figure (Bambu Lab, read 2026-11-16)", 'other': "72 dB in 3D Printed Decor's 600-hour test (as reported by StarterBench)", 'price': '$349 (maker, 2026-11-16)'}, 'asin': 'B0CHDM8VVZ'}],
 "after": '\n<h2>What the differences mean</h2>\n<p>Dealectric does not test printers. Every reading below comes from a named tester or from the maker, and each derived figure shows its arithmetic. The testers used different rooms, meters and, mostly, unstated distances, so treat gaps of a few dB between testers as indicative; gaps of 10 dB or more hold up.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Kobra S1, claim vs measurement:</strong> 59.6 − 44 = 15.6 dB above Anycubic\'s Quiet-mode figure, and 59.6 − 46 = 13.6 dB above its Standard-mode figure.</li>\n<li><strong>Could distance explain it?</strong> Free-field sound falls about 6 dB per doubling of distance, so 40 cm → 1 m is 20 × log10(100 ÷ 40) = 8.0 dB. Even if igor\'sLAB measured the Kobra S1 at 40 cm, as it did the P1S, that is 59.6 − 8.0 ≈ 51.6 dB at 1 m, still 51.6 − 44 = 7.6 dB over Anycubic\'s 1 m figure.</li>\n<li><strong>Same tester, same site:</strong> igor\'sLAB read the P1S at 64.7 dB(A) and the Kobra S1 at 59.6 dB(A): 64.7 − 59.6 = 5.1 dB apart.</li>\n<li><strong>Centauri Carbon 2 vs Kobra S1:</strong> 59.6 − 47 = 12.6 dB between the Kobra S1\'s reading and the top of Notebookcheck\'s CC2 average (different testers).</li>\n<li><strong>P2S vs P1S:</strong> 72 − 65 = 7 dB quieter in the same 3D Printed Decor test.</li>\n<li><strong>Add-on boxes add noise:</strong> QIDI Q2 with QIDI Box 65 − 56 = 9 dB louder (androidpctv); Anycubic\'s own ACE 2 Pro rating is 48 − 44 = 4 dB above the printer\'s Quiet-mode figure, and 55 − 44 = 11 dB above it while drying.</li>\n</ul>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Your apartment use</th><th>Best fit</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td>Printer in the room you live in, PLA and PETG</td><td>Elegoo Centauri Carbon 2 (lowest named measurement, 44–47 dB)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>You want Bambu\'s software and multi-color system</td><td>Bambu Lab P2S (65 dB vs the P1S\'s 72 dB in one test; under 50 dB in Silent Mode at 1 m per Bambu)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>ABS or ASA with an actively heated 65 °C chamber, printer behind a closed door</td><td>QIDI Q2 (56 dB measured) {buy:qidi-q2}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Smaller single-color parts with a HEPA + carbon filter</td><td>Flashforge Adventurer 5M Pro (maker\'s 50 dB low-noise figure, no independent reading) {buy:flashforge-adventurer-5m-pro}</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h2>Who measured what, and how</h2>\n<p><strong>Notebookcheck (Vineet Washington)</strong> measured the Elegoo Centauri Carbon 2 at an average of about 44–47 dB while printing, with peaks to 54 dB, and noted a mild, constant beep at idle. The review does not give the distance or print mode. Elegoo\'s own 45 dB comes from its lab with Elegoo PLA in Silent Mode and the auxiliary part-cooling fan off, so expect more noise on prints that need that fan.</p>\n<p><strong>igor\'sLAB (Tim Kutzner)</strong> is the only lab reading of the Anycubic Kobra S1: 59.6 dB(A) in operation, with no fans audible at idle. The same tester read the Bambu P1S at 64.7 dB(A) from about 40 cm in front of the closed door, and the open-frame Flashforge Adventurer 5M at 62.3 dB(A), mostly from its 3010 hotend fan. Anycubic\'s ≤44 dB is a 1 m figure in Quiet mode, and it carries the caveat that individual units may deviate.</p>\n<p><strong>3D Printed Decor</strong>, in a 600-hour three-printer test reported by StarterBench, measured the P1S at 72 dB and the P2S at 65 dB, with no distance given. Bambu\'s only published figure is for the P2S: below 50 dB in Silent Mode at 1 m. <strong>androidpctv</strong> measured the QIDI Q2 at 56 dB in normal use and 65 dB with the QIDI Box attached; QIDI publishes no noise figure for the Q2.</p>\n<p>Noise is only one apartment factor. If you print ABS or ASA, chamber heat matters too; see <a href="/enclosed-3d-printer-that-heats-up-fastest">which enclosed 3D printer heats up the fastest</a>.</p>\n<h2>Not recommended</h2>\n<p><strong>Buying the Anycubic Kobra S1 for its 44 dB figure.</strong> It is a printer-only, Quiet-mode, 1 m maker figure. The combo Anycubic sells in the US includes an ACE 2 Pro that Anycubic itself rates at 48 dB, or 55 dB while drying, and igor\'sLAB measured the combo at 59.6 dB(A) while printing. <strong>The Bambu Lab P1S</strong> is the loudest printer here in both tests that measured it (64.7 dB(A) at igor\'sLAB, 72 dB at 3D Printed Decor).</p>\n',
 "sources": [('Centauri Carbon 2 measured 44–47 dB average, 54 dB peaks, idle beep (Notebookcheck, 2026-03-02)', 'https://www.notebookcheck.net/Elegoo-Centauri-Carbon-2-3D-printer-review-Lot-of-features-for-not-a-lot-of-money.1239803.0.html'), ('Centauri Carbon 2 45 dB claim, its test conditions and price (Elegoo US, read 2026-11-16)', 'https://us.elegoo.com/products/centauri-carbon-2'), ("Kobra S1 Combo measured 59.6 dB(A) while printing (igor'sLAB, 2025-04-14)", 'https://www.igorslab.de/anycubic-kobra-s1-combo-im-test/6/'), ('Kobra S1 ≤44/≤46 dB at 1 m, ACE 2 Pro 48/55 dB at 1 m, price (Anycubic US, read 2026-11-16)', 'https://store.anycubic.com/products/kobra-s1-ace-2-pro-combo-3d-printer'), ("P1S measured 64.7 dB(A) at about 40 cm (igor'sLAB, 2023-10-12)", 'https://www.igorslab.de/bambu-lab-p1s-ams-combo-3d-drucker-im-test/6/'), ("P1S 72 dB and P2S 65 dB in 3D Printed Decor's 600-hour test (StarterBench, read 2026-11-16)", 'https://starterbench.com/vs/bambu-lab-p1s-vs-p2s'), ('P2S below 50 dB in Silent Mode, tested at 1 m (Bambu Lab wiki, read 2026-11-16)', 'https://wiki.bambulab.com/en/p2s/manual/p2s-faq'), ('P2S price, no dB figure on the store page (Bambu Lab US, read 2026-11-16)', 'https://us.store.bambulab.com/products/p2s'), ('P1S price, no dB figure on the store page (Bambu Lab US, read 2026-11-16)', 'https://us.store.bambulab.com/products/p1s'), ('QIDI Q2 measured 56 dB, 65 dB with QIDI Box (androidpctv, 2025-08-28)', 'https://androidpctv.com/qidi-q2-qidi-box-review'), ('QIDI Q2 product page: 65 °C chamber heating, no dB figure (QIDI, read 2026-11-16)', 'https://qidi3d.com/products/qidi-q2'), ("Adventurer 5M measured 62.3 dB(A) printing, 41.1 idle, 54.8 with hotend fan (igor'sLAB, 2025-02-27)", 'https://www.igorslab.de/flashforge-adventurer-5m-3d-drucker-im-test/6/'), ('Adventurer 5M Pro 50 dB low-noise, 55 dB standard (Flashforge, read 2026-11-16)', 'https://www.flashforge.com/products/adventurer-5m-pro-3d-printer'), ('About 6 dB per doubling of distance; readings at 0.5 m vs 2 m (Additive Realm, read 2026-11-16)', 'https://additiverealm.com/quietest-3d-printer-ranked-noise/')],
 "published": '2026-11-16',
 "checked": '2026-11-16',
 "updated": '2026-11-16',
 "all_links": True,
 "keep_pick": True},

